bol"}] :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $\left\vert\dfrac{x-1}{6}\right\vert \leq 1$." :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value.

The inequality specifies every number

$$
\dfrac{x-1}{6}
$$

whose distance from zero is less than or equal to $1$. This corresponds to the following compound inequality:

$$
-1 \leq \dfrac{x-1}{6} \leq 1
$$

Now, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.

$$
\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \le \frac{x - 1}{6} \le 1 \\ -6 & \le x - 1 \le 6 \\ -5 & \le x \le 7\end{bmatrix}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186048267} {:db/id 17592186050734} {:db/id 17592186069130 :question/id #uuid "6dccebba-e685-5ccf-8a2e-1661e84941a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-215464"} {:db/id 17592186069131 :question/id #uuid "b467536f-aa10-576c-a9c6-ed66bbafee39" :question/math-academy-id "q-215466"} {:db/id 17592186069289 :question/id #uuid "b089f476-27d3-575d-9dec-95701d683ed8" :question/math-academy-id "q-3673"} {:db/id 17592186068718 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186068510 :question/id #uuid "12d8aea9-62dd-5181-bd6e-54c11eba4152" :question/math-academy-id "e-14708"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186069132 :question/id #uuid "fcb879da-1b24-57e1-8cf8-e1e6de6fe967" :question/math-academy-id "q-215482"} {:db/id 17592186069133 :question/id #uuid "0ceea8c0-f989-54a6-9f70-92e530683a94" :question/math-academy-id "q-215489"} {:db/id 17592186069294 :question/id #uuid "848ad56e-2e24-5fe8-bf66-9dcd62c41f20" :question/math-academy-id "q-3693"}] :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative"} {:db/id 17592186068510 :question/id #uuid "12d8aea9-62dd-5181-bd6e-54c11eba4152" :question/math-academy-id "e-14708" :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id 17592186068718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative"}] :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $\vert 10 - 2x \vert +1 < 5$." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the inequality:

$$
\begin{vmatrix}10 - 2x & + 1\end{vmatrix}< 5; \mid 10 - 2x \mid \mid < 4
$$

Now, we convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value.

The inequality specifies every number $10-2x$ whose distance from zero is less than $4$. This corresponds to the following compound inequality:

$$
-4 < 10 - 2x < 4
$$

Now, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)

$$
\begin{bmatrix}-4 < 10 - 2x & < 4 \\ -14 < - 2x & < - 6 \\ 14 > 2x & > 6 \\ 7 > x & > 3\end{bmatrix}
$$

To make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the smaller number is on the left:

$$
3 < x < 7
$$"} {:db/id 17592186069132 :question/id #uuid "fcb879da-1b24-57e1-8cf8-e1e6de6fe967" :question/math-academy-id "q-215482"} {:db/id 17592186069133 :question/id #uuid "0ceea8c0-f989-54a6-9f70-92e530683a94" :question/math-academy-id "q-215489" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186068718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "ab4ce6ab-f572-536f-b69b-26107e70c78f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186066143} {:answer-field/id #uuid "1c0a61e3-aadd-51f2-af52-df568c7fa6e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186066144} {:answer-field/id #uuid "48a7fd8b-fc8e-504d-805e-8ece07aca323" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186066145}] :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $1 + \mid 17 - 3h \mid \le 9$. {{field-1}} {{field-2}}
