**Note:** The statement above encompasses two theorems:

- The **isosceles triangle theorem**:

*If a triangle is isosceles, then the base angles are congruent.*

- The **converse isosceles triangle theorem**: 

*If two angles in a triangle have the same measure, then the triangle must be isosceles.*" :tutorial/id #uuid "87d68609-ccd1-5ebd-b129-2c6993e05b75" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2227 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "5440fe87-c485-5fa7-ab27-be4de4746fa1" :step/math-academy-id 164419 :step/next {:db/id 17592186106628}} {:db/id 17592186106628 :step/content {:db/id 17592186105738 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186105525 :question/id #uuid "df6c46c7-a65c-578c-a9b3-e75de73c527a" :question/math-academy-id "e-2718"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d46a44-0f02-5491-8e71-2eb22ad50ff9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049949}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186106166} {:db/id 17592186106170} {:db/id 17592186505752} {:db/id 17592186505835}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of an Angle Using the Isosceles Triangle Theorem"} :step/id #uuid "6c37fcdd-4a4f-5fa4-b419-cdfb144ce00e" :step/math-academy-id 164420 :step/next {:db/id 17592186106629}} {:db/id 17592186106629 :step/content {:db/id 17592186105739 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186105526 :question/id #uuid "c7ae19b8-aee0-5a64-b7c8-61f3ce75272c" :question/math-academy-id "e-2721"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0690d62b-432c-5d1e-96f2-b43393f6efa9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048764} {:db/id 17592186050410}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186106167} {:db/id 17592186106171} {:db/id 17592186505731} {:db/id 17592186505815}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of an Angle in an Isosceles Triangle Given an Exterior Angle"} :step/id #uuid "52480c3c-c289-5e97-b7aa-1a5401a73156" :step/math-academy-id 164423 :step/next {:db/id 17592186106630}} {:db/id 17592186106630 :step/content {:db/id 17592186105740 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186105584 :question/id #uuid "d9e953e1-5af0-55eb-a861-af6f4ed9b720" :question/math-academy-id "e-4269"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9c2b7ee-d32b-550b-b110-81d04d75