${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}-2xy & 2y-{x}^{2}\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\to R,$ given by

$$
f:{{\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),
$$

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}-2xy & 2y-{x}^{2}\end{bmatrix},$ 
 we must have

$$
\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-2xy,\,\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y-{x}^{2}.
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2xy)=-2y\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y-{x}^{2})=-2x \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2xy)=-2x\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y-{x}^{2})=2\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}-2y & -2x \\ -2x & 2\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we evaluate this matrix at $(2,1).$ This gives

$$
{f}^{″}(2,1)=\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\ -4 & 2\end{bmatrix}.
$$"} {:db/id 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186157001 :question/id #uuid "53ca572c-798a-5529-9702-df3291a2b500" :question/math-academy-id "e-12523"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049044}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186157792 :question/id #uuid "56bfdc28-d81a-5ee4-a9f9-1fab676af72b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80944"} {:db/id 17592186157793 :question/id #uuid "292a0e8c-cdb2-548d-8ab3-a1c288439002" :question/math-academy-id "q-81029"} {:db/id 17592186235547 :question/id #uuid "06db9379-5030-59c8-9740-a48aa44cf00c" :question/math-academy-id "q-168867"} {:db/id 17592186237927 :question/id #uuid "ba2b3d0e-8f3a-5211-b064-2ffdb4af104d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102688"} {:db/id 17592186284389 :question/id #uuid "1ed19a02-b52e-57ba-89d7-67df43752d50" :question/math-academy-id "q-163641"} {:db/id 17592186284390 :question/id #uuid "64116d30-10df-5392-b872-327ec4131913" :question/math-academy-id "q-163642"} {:db/id 17592186284391 :question/id #uuid "9f138cc5-4903-5e5d-bf77-73940588090b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163643"} {:db/id 17592186351196 :question/id #uuid "0dab700a-fa4f-5675-9473-37a2b428ee20" :question/math-academy-id "q-81023"} {:db/id 17592186430448 :question/id #uuid "f2460b1b-0ae3-5791-81e8-e644fac55aa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-102692"} {:db/id 17592186435395 :question/id #uuid "e525b492-a29a-585f-8c96-2055a51f2341" :question/math-academy-id "q-102686"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"} {:db/id 17592186157001 :question/id #uuid "53ca572c-798a-5529-9702-df3291a2b500" :question/math-academy-id "e-12523" :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/problem "Given that 
![](images/43/43ec08d3ac9a00921335912f8e2cf8770397f141b4eebbb4f857fd0be69f7441.svg) 
 evaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \mathbb R^n \to \mathbb R,$ given by
![](images/39/398ea92d21b959026a702db0f606915acb31906451a9039925518ca79fa89717.svg)

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

![](images/5e/5ea286680d2cec429fe920628617d083f47dd53519c2d40f30115dee45a18bc3.svg)

The Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:

$$
H(\mathbf x) = \det \left( \boldsymbol{f}''(\mathbf x) \right)
$$

In our case, we have

![](images/14/1488754e319066706880b21fd4642c7b6a75a458770cab254b974b13d35425a2.svg)

First, notice that since ![](images/c9/c92e0f35c58187af3fe961947e6e96f0cd82cf32bb00cfd4f51ca3c742339e0c.svg) we must have

$$
\dfrac{\partial f}{\partial x} = \ln y, 
\qquad 
\dfrac{\partial f}{\partial y} = \dfrac xy.
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=0\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(\frac{x}{y})=\frac{1}{y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\frac{1}{y}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(\frac{x}{y})=-\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}0 & \frac{1}{y} \\ \frac{1}{y} & -\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$



Evaluating the second derivative at $(0,1),$ we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,1)=\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\ 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we have

$$
H(0,1) = 0 \cdot 0 - 1\cdot 1 = -1.
$$"} {:db/id 17592186049044} {:db/id 17592186157792 :question/id #uuid "56bfdc28-d81a-5ee4-a9f9-1fab676af72b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80944" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fac2aac-15fd-5b1a-8c19-cdbaaa605b1f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id 17592186155674} {:answer/id #uuid "af2543c6-e121-548c-9ce8-bd9e83f27959" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id 17592186155675} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1bd87c-c87b-5317-bf18-04917ad67fe4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id 17592186155676} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd64df2-e5b8-5aaa-a2df-8978d2413927" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id 17592186155677} {:answer/id #uuid "540f5941-edc3-564d-ab1c-16a630b65ad4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id 17592186155678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fd64df2-e5b8-5aaa-a2df-8978d2413927" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id 17592186155677} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7f08daa-f6b4-563b-b34a-95db72823c43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186155673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "Given that 
${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{3} & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\end{bmatrix},$
evaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\to R,$ given by

$$
f:{{\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),
$$

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

The Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:

$$
H(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{3} & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\end{bmatrix},$ we must have

$$
\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{3},\,\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{3})=2{y}^{3}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6x{y}^{2} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{3})=6x{y}^{2}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6{x}^{2}y\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{3} & 6x{y}^{2} \\ 6x{y}^{2} & 6{x}^{2}y\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$



Evaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\ 6 & 6\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we have

$$
H(1,1)=2\cdot 6-6\cdot 6=-24.
$$"} {:db/id 17592186157793 :question/id #uuid "292a0e8c-cdb2-548d-8ab3-a1c288439002" :question/math-academy-id "q-81029"} {:db/id 17592186235547 :question/id #uuid "06db9379-5030-59c8-9740-a48aa44cf00c" :question/math-academy-id "q-168867"} {:db/id 17592186237927 :question/id #uuid "ba2b3d0e-8f3a-5211-b064-2ffdb4af104d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102688" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62d58fc9-233d-5a98-9f47-8a3790a441f3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{\pi }^{2}" :db/id 17592186236443} {:answer/id #uuid "804c671d-3217-5280-aa02-fe2a73812ecc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186236615} {:answer/id #uuid "88c43743-4bdd-5d6d-8482-949f26f0705c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186236672} {:answer/id #uuid "944e0f31-80d6-5eac-8960-7ada905bec43" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{\pi }^{2}" :db/id 17592186236758} {:answer/id #uuid "d93bce69-5901-5324-bd97-83116ddf04a3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\pi }^{2}" :db/id 17592186237192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88c43743-4bdd-5d6d-8482-949f26f0705c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186236672} :answer-field/id #uuid "77c1b5e6-8017-5a27-ad73-0d376c902134" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186237601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "Given that 
