the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

The Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:

$$
H(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, notice that since
${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}y\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & x\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\end{bmatrix},$
we must have

$$
\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),\,\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=-{y}^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=-{x}^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}-{y}^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) & \operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\ \operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) & -{x}^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$



Evaluating the second derivative at $(\pi ,-1),$ we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(\pi ,-1)=\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\ -1 & 0\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we have

$$
H(\pi ,-1)=0\cdot 0-(-1)\cdot (-1)=-1.
$$"} {:db/id 17592186284389 :question/id #uuid "1ed19a02-b52e-57ba-89d7-67df43752d50" :question/math-academy-id "q-163641"} {:db/id 17592186284390 :question/id #uuid "64116d30-10df-5392-b872-327ec4131913" :question/math-academy-id "q-163642"} {:db/id 17592186284391 :question/id #uuid "9f138cc5-4903-5e5d-bf77-73940588090b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163643"} {:db/id 17592186351196 :question/id #uuid "0dab700a-fa4f-5675-9473-37a2b428ee20" :question/math-academy-id "q-81023" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a863fee-48cb-518a-94c7-332f0d5dfb90" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id 17592186348671} {:answer/id #uuid "236352e1-e284-5137-93e8-01d0c0b82dd3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id 17592186348749} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6da9cd-0b80-5391-a066-ff87ff441cbe" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id 17592186350254} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b5d5ad-403a-5e9b-b47e-9495ed54eecd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id 17592186350322} {:answer/id #uuid "da828216-6cb2-53d2-9a0c-74a4b4c5a870" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id 17592186350365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da828216-6cb2-53d2-9a0c-74a4b4c5a870" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id 17592186350365} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f56bbbf-1a13-5c6d-a2d7-69c5469daa32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186350734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "Given that 
