evaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\to R,$ given by

$$
f:{{\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),
$$

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

The Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:

$$
H(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}2(x-1){y}^{2} & 2(x-1)^{2}y\end{bmatrix},$ we must have

$$
\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2(x-1){y}^{2},\,\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2(x-1)^{2}y.
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=4(x-1)y \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=4(x-1)y\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=2(x-1)^{2}\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{2} & 4(x-1)y \\ 4(x-1)y & 2(x-1)^{2}\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$



Evaluating the second derivative at $(0,1),$ we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,1)=\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\ -4 & 2\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we have

$$
H(0,1)=2\cdot 2-(-4)\cdot (-4)=-12.
$$"} {:db/id 17592186430448 :question/id #uuid "f2460b1b-0ae3-5791-81e8-e644fac55aa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-102692" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b6147f2-99cb-5e0e-bfe7-1ab9fcb4bfaf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id 17592186430425} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd5f2d0-f063-5f9a-8554-0e38b366ddee" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186430426} {:answer/id #uuid "4c3b39c3-ebcc-501e-bf32-f62c8ab6fbca" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id 17592186430428} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8b4808-0307-5f43-b835-eaa5d7c78ac1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186430432} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d3bd0b-8f50-5fda-8e7a-df552a252f05" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186430436}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186430425} :answer-field/id #uuid "57597420-75c9-5305-b6c7-82cc31ede092" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186430440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "Given that 
${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} & 2y\operatorname{ln}⁡x\end{bmatrix},$ 
evaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\to R,$ given by

$$
f:{{\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),
$$

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

The Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:

$$
H(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, notice that since
${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} & 2y\operatorname{ln}⁡x\end{bmatrix},$
we must have

$$
\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\frac{{y}^{2}}{x},\,\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y\operatorname{ln}⁡x.
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=-\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\frac{2y}{x} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=\frac{2y}{x}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=2\operatorname{ln}⁡x\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & \frac{2y}{x} \\ \frac{2y}{x} & 2\operatorname{ln}⁡x\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$



Evaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\ 2 & 0\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we have

$$
H(1,1)=(-1)\cdot 0-2\cdot 2=-4.
$$"} {:db/id 17592186435395 :question/id #uuid "e525b492-a29a-585f-8c96-2055a51f2341" :question/math-academy-id "q-102686" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012e8862-6d84-5ca3-808d-e580b5b68412" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id 17592186435375} {:answer/id #uuid "1d97894b-06e8-5458-afce-3b6280583bcd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id 17592186435377} {:answer/id #uuid "49af7f88-d313-53b2-a836-26eef4f823e6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id 17592186435381} {:answer/id #uuid "6341ade3-f46e-594c-b2db-483df7d6f5cd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id 17592186435383} {:answer/id #uuid "e9393f5b-f485-5c2a-b52d-4ac15221029b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id 17592186435387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "012e8862-6d84-5ca3-808d-e580b5b68412" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id 17592186435375} :answer-field/id #uuid "835cf471-5984-50ad-ac7a-5c92395f40c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186435392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "Given that 
${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{2} & 2y{x}^{2}-1\end{bmatrix},$ 
evaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\to R,$ given by

$$
f:{{\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),
$$

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

The Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:

$$
H(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, notice that since
${f}^{′}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{2} & 2y{x}^{2}-1\end{bmatrix},$ we must have

$$
\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{2},\,\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y{x}^{2}-1.
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y{x}^{2}-1)=4xy \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2})=4xy\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{x}^{2}-1)=2{x}^{2}\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\ 4xy & 2{x}^{2}\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$



Evaluating the second derivative at $(1,-1),$ we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,-1)=\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\ -4 & 2\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we have

$$
H(1,-1)=2\cdot 2-(-4)\cdot (-4)=-12.
$$"} {:db/id 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186157002 :question/id #uuid "235325ea-4a42-5f63-974a-edd459a4a771" :question/math-academy-id "e-12524"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186157541 :question/id #uuid "cd7463fc-6818-5da6-ab8a-b593c73ec670" :question/math-academy-id "q-102699"} {:db/id 17592186157790 :question/id #uuid "1fc495d4-08fa-5ada-9f41-a42761e42726" :question/math-academy-id "q-80939"} {:db/id 17592186351225 :question/id #uuid "9e5fb489-dfa6-50c2-a270-dc2d65f25d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-81111"} {:db/id 17592186351229 :question/id #uuid "235e87ab-40f0-5bca-9e1d-4479ce5e2de8" :question/math-academy-id "q-81119"} {:db/id 17592186351230 :question/id #uuid "e0469958-83f9-5c79-aae7-bbff4a96354f" :question/math-academy-id "q-81123"} {:db/id 17592186394105 :question/id #uuid "5b55b18c-139d-56b5-94eb-26aeb293ef39" :question/math-academy-id "q-80947"} {:db/id 17592186430445 :question/id #uuid "98de8580-5081-5c82-af81-6826d2545a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-102461"} {:db/id 17592186430446 :question/id #uuid "a4a0c4af-3f1c-5b85-b0c9-4604955ba8b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-102698"} {:db/id 17592186481414 :question/id #uuid "c02d4f47-274a-5db8-9775-386bac66028f" :question/math-academy-id "q-102684"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"} {:db/id 17592186157002 :question/id #uuid "235325ea-4a42-5f63-974a-edd459a4a771" :question/math-academy-id "e-12524" :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/problem "Find $\boldsymbol f''(1,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)  = x^2 e^y.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \mathbb R^n \to \mathbb R,$ given by
![](images/f2/f2e3cce8b785350e4a3d746dfbbb1e805cc490c5a28680a59bb22e266b9c6b48.svg)

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

![](images/43/43938aea0610386ae1e7cd862b234b326a396a3c06df1cd8d63ba568c9bd5d62.svg)

In our case, we have

![](images/81/81b814aff57a058f564080308dd8fbe220994cf0dcbd84b80715ded32c5c96a1.svg)

First, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \frac{∂f}{∂y}\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{y}) & \frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}2x{e}^{y} & {x}^{2}{e}^{y}\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\text{ }\,{e}^{y})=2\text{ }\,{e}^{y}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})=2x\text{ }\,{e}^{y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\text{ }\,{e}^{y})=2x\text{ }\,{e}^{y}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})={x}^{2}{e}^{y}\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}2\text{ }\,{e}^{y} & 2x\text{ }\,{e}^{y} \\ 2x\text{ }\,{e}^{y} & {x}^{2}{e}^{y}\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we evaluate this matrix at $\left(1,0\right).$ This gives

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,0)=\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\ 2 & 1\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186157541 :question/id #uuid "cd7463fc-6818-5da6-ab8a-b593c73ec670" :question/math-academy-id "q-102699" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fca28ad-f59e-5a0a-bb4c-0662386d1e94" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\ -1 & 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186480829} {:answer/id #uuid "3075a971-db98-5b66-a3d1-9af12fdf7be7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\ -1 & 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186480831} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb3995c-cc62-5136-82b2-472b0cb824be" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\ 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186481006} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ef3863-4e52-56dd-9984-66598e15e8ff" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\ 1 & 1\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186481130} {:answer/id #uuid "dc10b03f-56c5-527c-94f1-47709864755a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\ 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186481155}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186481006} :answer-field/id #uuid "28c26c69-61cb-5d08-9210-43f100a3d7fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186153490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486} :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(1,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)=xy-{x}^{2}{y}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\to R,$ given by

$$
f:{{\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),
$$

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \frac{∂f}{∂y}\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-{x}^{2}{y}^{3}) & \frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-{x}^{2}{y}^{3})\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}y-2x{y}^{3} & x-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-2x{y}^{3})=-2{y}^{3}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=1-6x{y}^{2} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-2x{y}^{3})=1-6x{y}^{2}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=-6{x}^{2}y\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}-2{y}^{3} & 1-6x{y}^{2} \\ 1-6x{y}^{2} & -6{x}^{2}y\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,0).$ This gives

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,0)=\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\ 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186157790 :question/id #uuid "1fc495d4-08fa-5ada-9f41-a42761e42726" :question/math-academy-id "q-80939" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae64ecf2-f100-5ee1-bf22-d62f17c06d20" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}y\cos x & 0 \\ 0 & -x\sin y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186155662} {:answer/id #uuid "195c549d-45b4-55f3-a403-f4ee843b6e1b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 & \cos y + 1 \\ \cos y + 1 & -x\sin y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186155663} {:answer/id #uuid "30a4bd7f-a653-586c-8d6c-48bbd5f3eadf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 & \cos y + x \\ \cos y + x & \sin y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186155664} {:answer/id #uuid "6b54a19a-e583-584b-a065-7c3d2342cae8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \cos y + 1 \\ \cos y + 1 & x\cos y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186155665} {:answer/id #uuid "7613ab91-83d0-595d-baf0-b61833c485f3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}y\cos x & 1 \\ 1 & -x\sin y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186155666}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5f160e6d-8669-5f1d-a718-6927812f7f8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186155661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48011387-df7d-5d71-b876-3df593d3bf4e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\ \operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & x\operatorname{cos}⁡y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186394100} {:answer/id #uuid "b379f4c6-96cf-5dd6-9925-574eea16f8e0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}y\operatorname{cos}⁡x & 0 \\ 0 & -x\operatorname{sin}⁡y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186394101} {:answer/id #uuid "0e3f1c3c-63fa-5e17-875f-c1a698e0f6ed" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 & \operatorname{cos}⁡y+x \\ \operatorname{cos}⁡y+x & \operatorname{sin}⁡y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186394102} {:answer/id #uuid "6f9bcc3c-bd3b-5708-8734-2c02467d117b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 & \operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\ \operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & -x\operatorname{sin}⁡y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186394103} {:answer/id #uuid "3213b7e4-ef64-5dfb-891d-c56e3a6c1087" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}y\operatorname{cos}⁡x & 1 \\ 1 & -x\operatorname{sin}⁡y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186394104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f9bcc3c-bd3b-5708-8734-2c02467d117b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 & \operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\ \operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & -x\operatorname{sin}⁡y\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186394103} :answer-field/id #uuid "35959f64-1830-5289-be56-634cfb3973ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186394099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)=x\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\to R,$ given by

$$
f:{{\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),
$$

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \frac{∂f}{∂y}\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy) & \frac{∂}{∂y}(x\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy)\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y & x\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y)=0\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x)=\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y)=\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x)=-x\operatorname{sin}⁡y\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}0 & \operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\ \operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & -x\operatorname{sin}⁡y\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186351225 :question/id #uuid "9e5fb489-dfa6-50c2-a270-dc2d65f25d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-81111"} {:db/id 17592186351229 :question/id #uuid "235e87ab-40f0-5bca-9e1d-4479ce5e2de8" :question/math-academy-id "q-81119"} {:db/id 17592186351230 :question/id #uuid "e0469958-83f9-5c79-aae7-bbff4a96354f" :question/math-academy-id "q-81123" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c42b794-72d6-514f-85b6-40ef2b7dcd98" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\ 2 & 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186348690} {:answer/id #uuid "3454730a-5aab-57e6-8c0f-17209a604055" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\ 0 & 2\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186348916} {:answer/id #uuid "7b479b77-d903-5f0c-8f7d-530e7863b915" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\ 2 & -1\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186349579} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f41cb7-2e5a-5303-bc84-7130dab8c440" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\ -1 & 2\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186350611} {:answer/id #uuid "fb35d3bb-cccc-50cf-84a5-4d39d7149a97" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\ -2 & 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186350661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb35d3bb-cccc-50cf-84a5-4d39d7149a97" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\ -2 & 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186350661} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb30829b-8d9a-5a87-b3fc-44d8886af1ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186351029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(-1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)=(y-1)({x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\to R,$ given by

$$
f:{{\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),
$$

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \frac{∂f}{∂y}\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂}{∂x}((y-1)({x}^{2}-1)) & \frac{∂}{∂y}((y-1)({x}^{2}-1))\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}2x(y-1) & {x}^{2}-1\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x(y-1))=2(y-1)\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-1)=2x \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x(y-1))=2x\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-1)=0\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}2(y-1) & 2x \\ 2x & 0\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we evaluate this matrix at $(-1,2).$ This gives

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1,2)=\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\ -2 & 0\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186394105 :question/id #uuid "5b55b18c-139d-56b5-94eb-26aeb293ef39" :question/math-academy-id "q-80947"} {:db/id 17592186430445 :question/id #uuid "98de8580-5081-5c82-af81-6826d2545a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-102461"} {:db/id 17592186430446 :question/id #uuid "a4a0c4af-3f1c-5b85-b0c9-4604955ba8b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-102698"} {:db/id 17592186481414 :question/id #uuid "c02d4f47-274a-5db8-9775-386bac66028f" :question/math-academy-id "q-102684" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93574e00-8aff-52c2-8fef-8d24d76bb02a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\ 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186481016} {:answer/id #uuid "aee9d420-4960-50a5-922a-c43137c76d7d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\ 1 & -2\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186481067} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4a4294-c877-56f6-bfd0-3109ee79c13c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\ 1 & -4\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186481097} {:answer/id #uuid "c00142a0-9805-5734-8860-3bf5256f853f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\ -1 & -2\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186481104} {:answer/id #uuid "e631a5f0-8bc9-5fbb-b72c-fddfe67625ed" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\ 1 & -2\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186481177}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186481177} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cad98c5-f0af-530e-9545-f63d666cd3ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186481264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486} :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)=y\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\to R,$ given by

$$
f:{{\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),
$$

the second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\times n$ matrix

$$
{f}^{″}(x)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

In our case, we have

$$
{f}^{″}(x,y)=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

First, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \frac{∂f}{∂y}\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2}) & \frac{∂}{∂y}(y\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2})\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{y}{x} & \operatorname{ln}⁡x-2y\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Now, we compute the second partial derivatives:

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(\frac{y}{x})=-\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2y)=\frac{1}{x} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(\frac{y}{x})=\frac{1}{x}\, & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2y)=-2\end{aligned}
$$

So, the second derivative is

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \frac{1}{x} \\ \frac{1}{x} & -2\end{bmatrix}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,2).$ This gives

