uestion/id #uuid "19309cb7-ace3-5af0-908b-5924987e950f" :question/math-academy-id "q-312578"} {:db/id 17592186317276 :question/id #uuid "c15b3ea9-8f3d-5cc5-a69a-f9caee4c79da" :question/math-academy-id "q-342561"} {:db/id 17592186317277 :question/id #uuid "560351d2-9c68-5425-b187-0b2629e5a704" :question/math-academy-id "q-342562"} {:db/id 17592186317278 :question/id #uuid "4c8c7a88-6e10-5793-8076-5cf568ce9f31" :question/math-academy-id "q-342570"} {:db/id 17592186317279 :question/id #uuid "f2edf191-9bcb-50c6-bc5b-b3185f8280c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-342575"} {:db/id 17592186479082 :question/id #uuid "3e911702-eb82-5b97-88c2-1d3bfbe6d604" :question/math-academy-id "q-342576"} {:db/id 17592186479119 :question/id #uuid "b47ad43a-e012-58c2-b33a-c151f7cd3d62" :question/math-academy-id "q-342577"} {:db/id 17592186479132 :question/id #uuid "d295fd4d-8093-5953-9c94-5f7f1a143168" :question/math-academy-id "q-110128"} {:db/id 17592186487398 :question/id #uuid "f03606b0-4d82-587c-8251-04c53399de85" :question/math-academy-id "q-342572" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9f522c8-2e41-549d-a3cd-753ef997b9f0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186487000}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186487000} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bd876f7-79e5-597c-ac7b-34096cd74827" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186487154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "![](images/b1/b1735679cbf165e26ac22f1fd3076d450231ea8c20c1905ec74f008bc89ec33a.png)

The figure above shows the graph of a piecewise linear function $y=f(x).$ The point $A$ has coordinates $(1,2)$ and lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $(2,1)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ what is $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2)?$

$({f}^{-1})^{′}(2)=$
{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $(2,1)$ lies on ${f}^{-1},$ we have ${f}^{-1}(2)=1.$ 
The slope of the tangent to $f(x)$ for $x\in [0,4]$ is $-1$, hence, ${f}^{′}(1)=-1.$

The formula for the derivative of the inverse function is 

$$
({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.
$$

Evaluating at $x=2,$ we have

$$
\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(2) & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\  & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(1)} \\  & =\frac{1}{(-1)} \\  & =-1.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186064252 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186063998 :question/id #uuid "121d5f8c-3b38-5c75-aec1-646dc7d2f2f8" :question/math-academy-id "e-14719"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e05385-7cb6-5f21-b0d8-a7641d912d5b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048191}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186064618 :question/id #uuid "0e89d0fd-c938-54a1-9b82-cef992b23366" :question/math-academy-id "q-2294"} {:db/id 17592186064883 :question/id #uuid "59090c66-6332-5a45-a658-fc8034750491" :question/math-academy-id "q-5028"} {:db/id 17592186233516 :question/id #uuid "a3c782b0-333e-5ef5-97b8-c1749c597dee" :question/math-academy-id "q-15640"} {:db/id 17592186233648 :question/id #uuid "e896db88-7cab-5371-b88c-f834f9c54b36" :question/math-academy-id "q-2292"} {:db/id 17592186234120 :question/id #uuid "681d510c-bf12-5ea9-a7f5-ca72763e925a" :question/math-academy-id "q-5031"} {:db/id 17592186275185 :question/id #uuid "55ad62a1-4387-5fad-a8b0-2b49bf34cf69" :question/math-academy-id "q-14770"} {:db/id 17592186275348 :question/id #uuid "70eb040a-0b35-5385-90a6-1ec258e34a2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-15641"} {:db/id 17592186275349 :question/id #uuid "a174f217-0e4b-5a0f-9eec-2cc2635f6ebf" :question/math-academy-id "q-15646"} {:db/id 17592186275350 :question/id #uuid "3b8a373e-9fa1-5a8d-a43f-93c147067228" :question/math-academy-id "q-15647"} {:db/id 17592186275351 :question/id #uuid "8440be8d-9ebe-5dfc-9033-4f02294d7b13" :question/math-academy-id "q-15651"} {:db/id 17592186275352 :question/id #uuid "3c79a856-eb45-517a-9c06-a71c42d2d5df" :question/math-academy-id "q-15652"} {:db/id 17592186292542 :question/id #uuid "d2026ecc-ebf2-57c6-ab42-a50fb08ede36" :question/math-academy-id "q-2526"} {:db/id 17592186297350 :question/id #uuid "8004f487-3cf9-55ce-a70e-fc271afc0b4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-312579"} {:db/id 17592186297351 :question/id #uuid "3d10818b-b3a5-537c-a4e3-55ca3cdd0aba" :question/math-academy-id "q-312580"} {:db/id 17592186