14721"} {:db/id 17592186048813} {:db/id 17592186050961} {:db/id 17592186064525 :question/id #uuid "7605be7d-0ef8-5ee7-81b0-67250adac8b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-16097"} {:db/id 17592186064542 :question/id #uuid "34e33e76-2a83-5368-8561-def1a916040d" :question/math-academy-id "q-19201"} {:db/id 17592186233131 :question/id #uuid "9e508817-6e98-5a61-86b6-1bdfe91061a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-110234"} {:db/id 17592186234375 :question/id #uuid "1cbce8c7-b3f2-54f3-bf71-ca8aa949c9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-75829"} {:db/id 17592186234376 :question/id #uuid "2576954f-b0ee-571c-85ae-5533e6d22543" :question/math-academy-id "q-75836" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b25b7d1-2205-5d45-9eb4-1153c39f2254" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186486678} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf1ee9d-fb31-555f-8234-c02cee50db01" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{6}" :db/id 17592186486946} {:answer/id #uuid "cd994e00-b7e4-5872-9698-8e0bb1e9c264" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186487046} {:answer/id #uuid "f42704d7-ba6a-5ac9-b641-e73d8c7eb55c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id 17592186487116} {:answer/id #uuid "f70d98a5-70c4-581c-95be-04705131018f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{2}" :db/id 17592186487120}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186487046} :answer-field/id #uuid "401d966c-98a8-5ffc-958c-1d19edfa6b7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186487163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "The following table gives the values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(5).$

| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |
| --- | --- | --- |
| $3$ | $4$ | $9$ |
| $5$ | $1$ | $6$ |
| $8$ | $5$ | $4$ |" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is

$$
({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.
$$

Substituting $x=5,$ we have

$$
({f}^{-1})^{′}(5)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(5))}.
$$

From the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(5)=8$ and ${f}^{′}(8)=4.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(5) & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(5))} \\  & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(8)} \\  & =\frac{1}{4}.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186234377 :question/id #uuid "617c83ea-d0b1-50bd-8d58-f1a3cfb1e796" :question/math-academy-id "q-75838"} {:db/id 17592186247101 :question/id #uuid "1d3c2c96-95a0-5706-9edb-c677d76924c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-110272"} {:db/id 17592186247102 :question/id #uuid "19317eb2-2fe0-5251-9453-bd4bbec8a9f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-110279"} {:db/id 17592186247103 :question/id #uuid "32e90e8e-86b1-556f-b1e0-fc9bc969a8b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-110284" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0de97e9b-167d-58b8-b3d5-94d7072f96fc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id 17592186244438} {:answer/id #uuid "411a9d60-45d9-5255-af7c-f54d7ac9a709" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id 17592186244886} {:answer/id #uuid "7480aff9-21a8-5cfa-9c98-bc986f215b03" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{31}{5}" :db/id 17592186245351} {:answer/id #uuid "a3928f90-c565-5339-83c1-14d12d515196" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{44}{5}" :db/id 17592186245773} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d9aa97-30ab-5be0-9392-8e2eebc6259c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{3}{5}" :db/id 17592186246375}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186245351} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f27b98d-efdc-5fef-8552-5c0790435d8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186246742}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "The following table gives the values of $f(x),{f}^{′}(x),g(x),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1}\cdot g)^{′}(3)$ of the product of functions.

| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| $3$ | $2$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $-3$ |
| $-2$ | $3$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $2$ |" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is

$$
({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.
$$

Using this, and the product rule, the derivative of the function ${f}^{-1}(x)g(x)$ is

$$
({f}^{-1}\cdot g)^{′}(x)=\frac{g(x)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}+{g}^{′}(x){f}^{-1}(x).
$$

Substituting $x=3,$ we have

$$
({f}^{-1}\cdot g)^{′}(3)=\frac{g(3)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))}+{g}^{′}(3){f}^{-1}(3).
$$

From the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(3)=-2,$ $g(3)=-1,$ ${g}^{′}(3)=-3,$ and ${f}^{′}(-2)=-5.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1}\cdot g)^{′}(3) & =\frac{g(3)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))}+{g}^{′}(3){f}^{-1}(3) \\  & =\frac{-1}{{f}^{′}(-2)}+(-3)\cdot (-2) \\  & =\frac{-1}{-5}+6 \\  & =\frac{31}{5}.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186247108 :question/id #uuid "d16ade3b-ac3a-55c8-a501-f72a3071e370" :question/math-academy-id "q-110307"} {:db/id 17592186247109 :question/id #uuid "d4549623-c64d-5c74-90da-3e23faed0aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-110308"} {:db/id 17592186297353 :question/id #uuid "1edb97ff-e669-542c-ba07-6fedf01189b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-312583"} {:db/id 17592186297354 :question/id #uuid "1f15cb00-451b-5523-bf6f-8460aecf67b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-312584" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186064253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b492068c-2bd2-5611-baab-780959d24c3d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of an Inverse Function Using a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "521bb03d-1d14-507e-b5f1-abf1722f95ef" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id 17592186295739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "521bb03d-1d14-507e-b5f1-abf1722f95ef" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id 17592186295739} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3516820-e93c-50fa-892a-8f84d07c3eb5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186297035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "Find ${(g\cdot {f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)$ of the product of functions, given the following table of values of $f(x),{f}^{′}(x),g(x),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points.

