${(g\cdot {f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)=$
{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is

$$
({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.
$$

Using this, and the product rule, the derivative of the function $g(x){f}^{-1}(x)$ is

$$
(g\cdot {f}^{-1})^{′}(x)={g}^{′}(x){f}^{-1}(x)+\frac{g(x)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.
$$

Substituting $x=2,$ we have

$$
(g\cdot {f}^{-1})^{′}(2)={g}^{′}(2){f}^{-1}(2)+\frac{g(2)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}.
$$

From the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(2)=5,$ $g(2)=4,$ ${g}^{′}(2)=-3,$ and ${f}^{′}(5)=-1.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}(g\cdot {f}^{-1})^{′}(2) & ={g}^{′}(2){f}^{-1}(2)+\frac{g(2)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\  & =-3\cdot 5+\frac{4}{{f}^{′}(5)} \\  & =-15+\frac{4}{(-1)} \\  & =-15-4 \\  & =-19.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186317287 :question/id #uuid "8517d68d-8110-58f2-a065-5eed954b7e43" :question/math-academy-id "q-342588"} {:db/id 17592186317288 :question/id #uuid "cca80ae0-62ef-5413-ba41-4aa5821f7e48" :question/math-academy-id "q-342589"} {:db/id 17592186317289 :question/id #uuid "918f9438-aa6e-5a76-8250-20275f26c02d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342590"} {:db/id 17592186317290 :question/id #uuid "89938d94-24bb-5069-96de-7c0c5e9ce7ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-342591"} {:db/id 17592186317291 :question/id #uuid "2eeba335-8257-5e02-8c8c-83f41ecad374" :question/math-academy-id "q-342592"} {:db/id 17592186317292 :question/id #uuid "53ed59d8-b22e-538d-9cc1-0f9210effe07" :question/math-academy-id "q-342596" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be8b47e-8161-5ac6-af15-f112a84dd1b9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186315375}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186315375} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdde61d2-0b02-5fd6-a68f-661c818e9a55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186317033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "Find ${(g\cdot {f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)$ of the product of functions, given the following table of values of $f(x),{f}^{′}(x),g(x),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points.

