$$
{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}
$$

First, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(2).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(2)=x.$ For $x\ne \frac{1}{2},$ this gives

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(2) & =x \\ f(x) & =2 \\ \frac{3x+1}{2x-1} & =2 \\ \frac{3x+1}{2x-1}\cdot (2x-1) & =2\cdot (2x-1) \\ \frac{3x+1}{\cancel{(2x-1)}}\cdot \cancel{(2x-1)} & =4x-2 \\ 3x+1 & =4x-2 \\ 1+2 & =4x-3x \\ x & =3.\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, ${f}^{-1}(2)=3.$

Now we calculate ${f}^{′}(3),$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\frac{3x+1}{2x-1} \\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\frac{5}{(2x-1)^{2}} \\ {f}^{′}(3) & =-\frac{5}{{(2\cdot 3-1)}^{2}} \\  & =-\frac{5}{{(5)}^{2}} \\  & =-\frac{1}{5}\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2) & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\  & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(3)} \\  & =\frac{1}{(-\frac{1}{5})} \\  & =-5.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186234380 :question/id #uuid "5192c69f-4919-5288-bf42-2e9b36903c79" :question/math-academy-id "q-76113"} {:db/id 17592186247110 :question/id #uuid "697e17f6-464a-5495-90d8-1dc0fdda0186" :question/math-academy-id "q-110338" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d86fb7c-04a2-5054-88db-d87318f91df0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186245716} {:answer/id #uuid "a7efd507-c58e-56ec-8841-05d7624ba7c1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id 17592186245816} {:answer/id #uuid "b538f1e2-5740-5e86-9585-792990790c3e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{2}" :db/id 17592186245930} {:answer/id #uuid "cf18104f-33a0-52e9-88d9-69f208eb80ab" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186246163} {:answer/id #uuid "f4626bee-994c-50c4-b9f0-fb3dfa085a3e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186246468}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186246468} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b79bcdf-534b-5594-b18b-23bc8c71894d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186246735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486} :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\frac{x+10}{x+1}.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4).$" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4),$ we use the following formula:

