\left(f^{-1}\right)'(x) = \dfrac{1}{f'(f^{-1}(x))}
$$

To help remember this formula, note that it's okay to swap the derivative symbol (the prime) with the inverse symbol (the exponent of $-1$) as long as we take the reciprocal afterward." :tutorial/id #uuid "a1f70bcd-9b56-5fdd-ba18-58b625c05af0" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9132 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} {:db/id 17592186065126 :step/content {:db/id 17592186064251 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186063999 :question/id #uuid "d113528f-a3ff-5f28-b071-bcf355a36b45" :question/math-academy-id "e-14720"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4270c31c-80f1-5b5d-bca8-e16a47206c2b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048686} {:db/id 17592186049352}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186064519} {:db/id 17592186064520} {:db/id 17592186233936} {:db/id 17592186247085} {:db/id 17592186247086} {:db/id 17592186247096} {:db/id 17592186275370} {:db/id 17592186275375} {:db/id 17592186275377} {:db/id 17592186287889} {:db/id 17592186297349} {:db/id 17592186317276} {:db/id 17592186317277} {:db/id 17592186317278} {:db/id 17592186317279} {:db/id 17592186479082} {:db/id 17592186479119} {:db/id 17592186479132} {:db/id 17592186487398}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of an Inverse Function From a Graph"} :step/id #uuid "16c7f862-0b61-56ca-b731-b881c09a79a7" :step/math-academy-id 187681 :step/next {:db/id 17592186065127}} {:db/id 17592186065127 :step/content {:db/id 17592186064252 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186063998 :question/id #uuid "121d5f8c-3b38-5c75-aec1-646dc7d2f2f8" :question/math-academy-id "e-14719"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e05385-7cb6-5f21-b0d8-a7641d912d5b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048191}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186064618} {:db/id 17592186064883} {:db/id 17592186233516} {:db/id 17592186233648} {:db/id 17592186234120} {:db/id 17592186275185} {:db/id 17592186275348} {:db/id 17592186275349} {:db/id 17592186275350} {:db/id 17592186275351} {:db/id 17592186275352} {:db/i