$$"} :step/id #uuid "29ee00b7-02cb-5105-a7be-7bc30258a733" :step/next {:db/id 17592186487425}} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b25b7d1-2205-5d45-9eb4-1153c39f2254" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186486678} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf1ee9d-fb31-555f-8234-c02cee50db01" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{6}" :db/id 17592186486946} {:answer/id #uuid "cd994e00-b7e4-5872-9698-8e0bb1e9c264" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186487046} {:answer/id #uuid "f42704d7-ba6a-5ac9-b641-e73d8c7eb55c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id 17592186487116} {:answer/id #uuid "f70d98a5-70c4-581c-95be-04705131018f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{2}" :db/id 17592186487120}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186487046} :answer-field/id #uuid "401d966c-98a8-5ffc-958c-1d19edfa6b7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186487163} {:answer/id #uuid "2b25b7d1-2205-5d45-9eb4-1153c39f2254" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186486678} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf1ee9d-fb31-555f-8234-c02cee50db01" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{6}" :db/id 17592186486946} {:answer/id #uuid "cd994e00-b7e4-5872-9698-8e0bb1e9c264" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186487046} {:answer/id #uuid "f42704d7-ba6a-5ac9-b641-e73d8c7eb55c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id 17592186487116} {:answer/id #uuid "f70d98a5-70c4-581c-95be-04705131018f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{2}" :db/id 17592186487120} {:db/id 17592186487425 :step/content {:db/id 17592186234379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43858207-8831-5183-b09f-a3da1530cacd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{9}{5}" :db/id 17592186486740} {:answer/id #uuid "59d574d6-2cda-524f-ba83-6266f545c2b7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{5}{9}" :db/id 17592186486791} {:answer/id #uuid "64c98e51-6b85-5d4c-ac0f-82782d6de80e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{5}" :db/id 17592186486815} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e519cc-a7bd-5d74-8524-f56366c5b993" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id 17592186486975} {:answer/id #uuid "c27521f8-15fb-507d-92a2-e35438e66960" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186487022}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186486975} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c2d58ce-95e5-572a-9ac2-e040031c4dfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186487226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "10dcb0f4-5f0f-5b93-a598-6c0cd2ed4435" :question/math-academy-id "q-76105" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\frac{3x+1}{2x-1}.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2).$" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2),$ we use the following formula:

$$
{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}
$$

First, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(2).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(2)=x.$ For $x\ne \frac{1}{2},$ this gives

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(2) & =x \\ f(x) & =2 \\ \frac{3x+1}{2x-1} & =2 \\ \frac{3x+1}{2x-1}\cdot (2x-1) & =2\cdot (2x-1) \\ \frac{3x+1}{\cancel{(2x-1)}}\cdot \cancel{(2x-1)} & =4x-2 \\ 3x+1 & =4x-2 \\ 1+2 & =4x-3x \\ x & =3.\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, ${f}^{-1}(2)=3.$

Now we calculate ${f}^{′}(3),$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\frac{3x+1}{2x-1} \\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\frac{5}{(2x-1)^{2}} \\ {f}^{′}(3) & =-\frac{5}{{(2\cdot 3-1)}^{2}} \\  & =-\frac{5}{{(5)}^{2}} \\  & =-\frac{1}{5}\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2) & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\  & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(3)} \\  & =\frac{1}{(-\frac{1}{5})} \\  & =-5.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "53aab599-8ea7-5095-9e1f-104bd68f1330" :step/next {:db/id 17592186487430}} {:db/id 17592186487421 :step/content {:db/id 17592186317292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be8b47e-8161-5ac6-af15-f112a84dd1b9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186315375}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186315375} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdde61d2-0b02-5fd6-a68f-661c818e9a55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186317033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "53ed59d8-b22e-538d-9cc1-0f9210effe07" :question/math-academy-id "q-342596" :question/problem "Find ${(g\cdot {f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)$ of the product of functions, given the following table of values of $f(x),{f}^{′}(x),g(x),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points.

| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| $2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $\frac{1}{2}$ |
| $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $3$ | $-1$ |

${(g\cdot {f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)=$
{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is

$$
({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.
$$

Using this, and the product rule, the derivative of the function $g(x){f}^{-1}(x)$ is

$$
(g\cdot {f}^{-1})^{′}(x)={g}^{′}(x){f}^{-1}(x)+\frac{g(x)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.
$$

Substituting $x=2,$ we have

$$
(g\cdot {f}^{-1})^{′}(2)={g}^{′}(2){f}^{-1}(2)+\frac{g(2)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}.
$$

From the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(2)=1,$ $g(2)=-1,$ ${g}^{′}(2)=\frac{1}{2},$ and ${f}^{′}(1)=4.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}(g\cdot {f}^{-1})^{′}(2) & ={g}^{′}(2){f}^{-1}(2)+\frac{g(2)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\  & =\frac{1}{2}\cdot 1+\frac{(-1)}{{f}^{′}(1)} \\  & =\frac{1}{2}+\frac{(-1)}{4} \\  & =\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{4} \\  & =\frac{1}{4}.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "410fa10e-cbe7-5086-9bf0-1df3c0ba90fb"} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be8b47e-8161-5ac6-af15-f112a84dd1b9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186315375}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186315375} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdde61d2-0b02-5fd6-a68f-661c818e9a55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186317033} {:answer/id #uuid "2be8b47e-8161-5ac6-af15-f112a84dd1b9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186315375} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43858207-8831-5183-b09f-a3da1530cacd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{9}{5}" :db/id 17592186486740} {:answer/id #uuid "59d574d6-2cda-524f-ba83-6266f545c2b7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{5}{9}" :db/id 17592186486791} {:answer/id #uuid "64c98e51-6b85-5d4c-ac0f-82782d6de80e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{5}" :db/id 17592186486815} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e519cc-a7bd-5d74-8524-f56366c5b993" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id 17592186486975} {:answer/id #uuid "c27521f8-15fb-507d-92a2-e35438e66960" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186487022}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186486975} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c2d58ce-95e5-572a-9ac2-e040031c4dfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186487226} {:answer/id #uuid "43858207-8831-5183-b09f-a3da1530cacd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{9}{5}" :db/id 17592186486740} {:answer/id #uuid "59d574d6-2cda-524f-ba83-6266f545c2b7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{5}{9}" :db/id 17592186486791} {:answer/id #uuid "64c98e51-6b85-5d4c-ac0f-82782d6de80e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{5}" :db/id 17592186486815} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e519cc-a7bd-5d74-8524-f56366c5b993" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id 17592186486975} {:answer/id #uuid "c27521f8-15fb-507d-92a2-e35438e66960" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186487022} {:db/id 17592186487430 :step/content {:db/id 17592186487398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9f522c8-2e41-549d-a3cd-753ef997b9f0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186487000}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186487000} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bd876f7-79e5-597c-ac7b-34096cd74827" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186487154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f03606b0-4d82-587c-8251-04c53399de85" :question/math-academy-id "q-342572" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b1735679cbf165e26ac22f1fd3076d450231ea8c20c1905ec74f008bc89ec33a.png)

The figure above shows the graph of a piecewise linear function $y=f(x).$ The point $A$ has coordinates $(1,2)$ and lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $(2,1)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ what is $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2)?$

$({f}^{-1})^{′}(2)=$
{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $(2,1)$ lies on ${f}^{-1},$ we have ${f}^{-1}(2)=1.$ 
The slope of the tangent to $f(x)$ for $x\in [0,4]$ is $-1$, hence, ${f}^{′}(1)=-1.$

The formula for the derivative of the inverse function is 

$$
({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.
$$

Evaluating at $x=2,$ we have

$$
\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(2) & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\  & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(1)} \\  & =\frac{1}{(-1)} \\  & =-1.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "660230ab-1276-560d-bdd5-765d8d1b7e46" :step/next {:db/id 17592186487421}} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9f522c8-2e41-549d-a3cd-753ef997b9f0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186487000}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186487000} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bd876f7-79e5-597c-ac7b-34096cd74827" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186487154} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f522c8-2e41-549d-a3cd-753ef997b9f0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186487000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a9914a1-bd63-5503-bb36-c2533c2c5218" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{5}" :db/id 17592186063355} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc67312-c83d-5cab-b917-ee2161d29129" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186063356} {:answer/id #uuid "c283d4fd-1d67-5c92-a428-3fc3d98830e4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186063357} {:answer/id #uuid "cad706a5-f7c0-5286-9b96-bf0ba4a525c4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186063358} {:answer/id #uuid "de134615-356c-50aa-8b5e-53d741c02ca0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186063359}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186063356} :answer-field/id #uuid "5881a3d1-5740-518f-bfdd-3ac99c905e6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186063354} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9914a1-bd63-5503-bb36-c2533c2c5218" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{5}" :db/id 17592186063355} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc67312-c83d-5cab-b917-ee2161d29129" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186063356} {:answer/id #uuid "c283d4fd-1d67-5c92-a428-3fc3d98830e4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186063357} {:answer/id #uuid "cad706a5-f7c0-5286-9b96-bf0ba4a525c4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186063358} {:answer/id #uuid "de134615-356c-50aa-8b5e-53d741c02ca0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186063359} {:activity/course {:db/id 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id 17592186505883} :activity/id #uuid "895899f5-e0e0-50f3-bd94-fa13c6acacef" :activity/scope {:db/id 17592186048441 :topic/id #uuid "9faf7c3f-8d4f-5e48-97ed-6c10e2c5383a" :topic/math-academy-id 291} :activity/steps [{:db/id 17592186505862 :step/content {:db/id 17592186247110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d86fb7c-04a2-5054-88db-d87318f91df0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186245716} {:answer/id #uuid "a7efd507-c58e-56ec-8841-05d7624ba7c1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id 17592186245816} {:answer/id #uuid "b538f1e2-5740-5e86-9585-792990790c3e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{2}" :db/id 17592186245930} {:answer/id #uuid "cf18104f-33a0-52e9-88d9-69f208eb80ab" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186246163} {:answer/id #uuid "f4626bee-994c-50c4-b9f0-fb3dfa085a3e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186246468}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186246468} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b79bcdf-534b-5594-b18b-23bc8c71894d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186246735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "697e17f6-464a-5495-90d8-1dc0fdda0186" :question/math-academy-id "q-110338" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\frac{x+10}{x+1}.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4).$" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4),$ we use the following formula:

$$
{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(4)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))}
$$

First, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(4).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(4)=x.$ For $x\ne -1,$ this gives

$$
