$({f}^{-1})^{′}(2)=$
{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2),$ we use the following formula:

$$
{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)=\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}
$$

First, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(2).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(2)=x.$ This gives

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(2) & =x \\ f(x) & =2 \\ \sqrt{x} & =2 \\ x & ={2}^{2} \\ x & =4.\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, we have ${f}^{-1}(2)=4.$

Now, we calculate ${f}^{′}(4),$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\sqrt{x} \\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\frac{1}{2\sqrt{x}} \\ {f}^{′}(4) & =\frac{1}{2\sqrt{4}} \\ {f}^{′}(4) & =\frac{1}{4}\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2) & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\  & =\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(4)} \\  & =\frac{1}{(\frac{1}{4})} \\  & =4.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "d3f19cde-6964-5e90-b86b-fab6f1784841"} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "521f1d1c-c4a9-54ce-be0a-26a5043158cf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186505268}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186505268} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dc0e4ad-a39d-502a-8eb5-af62880a7035" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186505640} {:answer/id #uuid "521f1d1c-c4a9-54ce-be0a-26a5043158cf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186505268} {:db/id 17592186049849 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id 17592186428868 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account linear: 1 rises / 3 eligible passed source activities = 0.333333; nearest selected fraction = 1/3. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: linear=1/3 (1/3). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/linear-frequency-estimates.json, pair 3120->1970. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id 17592186048195} :encompassing/weight 0.3333333333333333} {:db/id 17592186428869 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account linear: 1 rises / 3 eligible passed source activities = 0.333333; nearest selected fraction = 1/3. Crossing activity numbers [3]; waits [3]. Separate account estimates: linear=1/3 (1/3). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activ