$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "6f731acb-e452-5433-88a5-1e2c66fd5a84" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6078 :tutorial/title "The Optimal Least-Squares Solution"} {:db/id 17592186163313 :tutorial/content "There are many ways to find the pseudoinverse of a given matrix $A.$ One way is to use the singular value decomposition of $A{:}$

Specifically, if 

$$
A=U \Sigma V ^T
$$

is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by

$$
