$$


where $\Sigma^+$ is the pseudoinverse of $\Sigma.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "bd110f79-cfe0-58f8-b7e6-ea9baa7814d9" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6102 :tutorial/title "Finding the Pseudoinverse Using Singular Value Decomposition"} {:db/id 17592186163314 :tutorial/content "For an *almost* zero ${\color{red}{m}}\times {\color{blue}{n}}$ matrix with non-zero entries 

$$
\sigma_1, \: \sigma_2, \: \ldots, \: \sigma_r
$$

on the main diagonal only, the corresponding pseudoinverse is the *almost* zero ${\color{blue}{n}}\times {\color{red}{m}}$ matrix with non-zero entries 

$$
{\sigma_1^{-1}}, \, {\sigma_2^{-1}}, \, \ldots, \, {\sigma_r^{-1}}
$$

on the main diagonal only.

For example, for the matrix $A,$ given by

![](images/d6/d6d6a167747f99c5a48be59ae3e11ca7b5a9188e80ddeb63b8c0f193d991b18c.svg)

we calculate its pseudoinverse as follows:

- **Step 1:** Replace the non-zero elements on the main diagonal with their multiplicative inverses.

- **Step 2:** Transpose the resulting matrix.

$$
\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & ={\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 4 & 0\end{bmatrix}}^{+} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}{3}^{-1} & 0 \\ 0 & {4}^{-1} \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}1/3 & 0 \\ 0 & 1/4 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\frac{1}{12}\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\ 0 & 3 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "8709222e-61fc-512e-82ff-3564c1513100" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6103 :tutorial/title "The Pseudoinverse of an Almost Diagonal Matrix"} {:activity/course {:db/id 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id 17592186420796} :activity/id #uuid "6fcc24e3-a2d7-5c60-8e6f-28eb1ce8232f" :activity/scope {:db/id 17592186049503 :topic/id #uuid "fa18866e-f310-5b54-8bcb-21e9073c9cde" :topic/math-academy-id 3134} :activity/steps [{:db/id 17592186420794 :step/content {:db/id 17592186420791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32c5eab7-61e5-58ba-983c-a7f55e21301d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{20}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 1 \\ 0 & 2 & -6\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186420765} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1203aa-43a1-5ff4-889a-1439cc8945c3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{20}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\ 0 & -6 & 2\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186420767} {:answer/id #uuid "73f62c7b-39b6-567c-8e60-5bf5c983d0c9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{20}\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 0 \\ 2 & -6 & 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186420772} {:answer/id #uuid "7e01a274-8738-5cf2-a673-1055c4c67b97" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{20}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\ 3 & 0 \\ -6 & 2\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186420775} {:answer/id #uuid "fb51fb6a-1738-5259-951f-347a4793bbda" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{20}\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 3 & 0 \\ -2 & 6\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186420783}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186420767} :answer-field/id #uuid "a01449e0-fee7-54b8-bc93-a094ffce75c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186420786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a18b0561-3c55-5481-a95c-144e99d62fb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-138620" :question/problem "$$
