ield/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186314456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/problem "$$
f(x)∼\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }{a}_{n}\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)
$$

Let $f(x)$ be the $2\pi $-periodic extension of a function from $x\in [-\pi ,\pi )$ to $x\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $4$th cosine Fourier coefficient of $f(-x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is

$$
f(x)∼\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }{a}_{n}\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).
$$

Recall that the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(-x)$ are

- ${a}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,

- ${a}_{n},$ $n\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and

- $-{b}_{n},$ $n\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.

