rs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84639246-60cf-50d4-874a-b2166ddf8829" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{1}{2} - \frac{e^{-x/2}}{2}" :db/id 17592186133285} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c60b0a-4da8-5fa8-93b6-45d924a57ba3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \frac{e^{-x/2}}{2}" :db/id 17592186133286} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e78026-6d4e-5180-baaf-d3fa1dae931e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{e^{-x/2}}{2} + \frac{1}{2}" :db/id 17592186133287} {:answer/id #uuid "5d0e3bb7-c3a7-5606-b66c-0257d6a52f35" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{e^{-x/2}}{2}" :db/id 17592186133288} {:answer/id #uuid "7d27c7df-0148-58fb-bf9f-35c06f77e520" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{e^{-x/2}}{2} - 1" :db/id 17592186133289}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d29670cd-928f-556c-8bb7-ed0713850686" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186133284}] :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function
$f(x) = \frac{e^{-\mid x/2 \mid}}{4}, x ∈ (- ∞, ∞)$,
its cumulative distribution function is
$F(x) = {\frac{e^{x/2}}{2},\begin{vmatrix}x < 0 \\ h(x),\end{vmatrix}x \ge 0$.
Find the function $h(x)$."} {:db/id 17592186419950 :question/id #uuid "aa0570cf-0a8d-5b19-8cfc-d1d338d11235" :question/math-academy-id "q-89631"} {:db/id 17592186419951 :question/id #uuid "ae38bc39-2bd5-58c3-af2b-ad65de482c6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-89635" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "095360e1-dd96-5383-931f-a201eff47a39" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x)=1-\frac{1}{1-{e}^{x}}" :db/id 17592186419857} {:answer/id #uuid "170a0edf-da7f-5652-903d-c47b4ac8c342" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x)=1+\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}}" :db/id 17592186419864} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8d1627-2737-5252-95ce-1a7d32a52868" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x)=1-\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}}" :db/id 17592186419871} {:answer/id #uuid "4b0ae796-f204-5f28-ae72-68cb7f93938e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x)=1+\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}" :db/id 17592186419873} {:answer/id #uuid "cfec970b-e672-5e0e-a27f-c56e83e7f7ee" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x)=1-\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}" :db/id 17592186419918}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186419918} :answer-field/id #uuid "f84d8dbb-e4a3-55af-a310-662430392d90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186419940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

$$
f(x)=\frac{2{e}^{x}}{(1+{e}^{x})^{3}},\,x\in (-\infty ,\infty ),
$$

find the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)={\int }_{-\infty }^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t.
$$

For the given probability density function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\int }_{-\infty }^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t \\  & ={\int }_{-\infty }^{x}\frac{2{e}^{t}}{(1+{e}^{t})^{3}}\,\text{d}t \\  & ={-\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{t})^{2}}|}_{-\infty }^{x} \\  & =-\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}+1 \\  & =1-\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186419956 :question/id #uuid "dbdaccde-7824-5d29-93f1-f05b495a99f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-126213"} {:db/id 17592186419958 :question/id #uuid "fb64e84b-4036-56ed-b5be-3b99c498406f" :question/math-academy-id "q-210762"} {:db/id 17592186424886 :question/id #uuid "2b70eaac-0c45-5da5-8a2f-2002d9071035" :question/math-academy-id "q-89727" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "492f777b-8264-55ab-9be1-d1359bd9513d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id 17592186424871} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7a5540-6762-5260-9b7f-2a98061bf95e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{4}" :db/id 17592186424872} {:answer/id #uuid "50e4b7f0-64ef-587b-bfde-a4520b836560" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id 17592186424873} {:answer/id #uuid "d60102cb-368c-5209-b3c3-06d9c44b89a2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{2}-\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id 17592186424880} {:answer/id #uuid "ef55c585-a616-50c9-9382-ffb7b5a8ceda" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id 17592186424881}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186424881} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce55fccd-c2b9-544b-881d-b59a7e7c0f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186424884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

$$
f(x)=\frac{{e}^{-|x/3|}}{6},\,x\in (-\infty ,\infty ),
$$

its cumulative distribution function is 

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2},\, & x<0 \\ h(x),\, & x\ge 0.\end{aligned}
$$

Find the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)=\{\begin{aligned}{\int }_{-\infty }^{x}\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\,\text{d}t, & x<0 \\ {\int }_{-\infty }^{0}\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\,\text{d}t+{\int }_{0}^{x}\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\,\text{d}t, & x\ge 0\end{aligned}
$$

Let's compute the integrals.

- If $x\le 0,$ we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{-\infty }^{x}\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\,\text{d}t & ={\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{2}|}_{-\infty }^{x} \\  & =\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2},\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{-\infty }^{0}\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\,\text{d}t & ={\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\  & =\frac{1}{2}.\end{aligned}
$$

- If $x>0,$ we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{0}^{x}\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\,\text{d}t & =-{\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\  & =-\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}+\frac{1}{2}.\end{aligned}
$$

As a result, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{-\infty }^{0}\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\,\text{d}t+{\int }_{0}^{x}\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\,\text{d}t & =\frac{1}{2}+(-\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}+\frac{1}{2}) \\  & =1-\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}.\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2}, & x<0 \\ 1-\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}, & x\ge 0.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186442323 :question/id #uuid "7e1280de-34a4-5310-b0ea-3ca5ec3ba975" :question/math-academy-id "q-210763" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65441b2f-7b3a-53c5-af33-45bf0ced0a21" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}" :db/id 17592186442310}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186442310} :answer-field/id #uuid "60abe397-ada8-52f7-89c3-1ccbe2f29023" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186442320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

