er-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186424883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

$$
f(x)=\{\begin{aligned}-\frac{2}{9}(x-1)(x-4),\, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 0,\, & \text{otherwise}\end{aligned}
$$

its cumulative distribution function is 

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0,\, & x<1 \\ h(x),\, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 1,\, & x>4.\end{aligned}
$$

Find the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $1\le x\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\ {\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4\end{aligned}
$$

For the given probability density function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t & ={\int }_{1}^{x}-\frac{2}{9}(t-1)(t-4)\,\text{d}t \\  & ={\int }_{1}^{x}-\frac{2}{9}({t}^{2}-5t+4)\,\text{d}t \\  & ={(-\frac{2}{27}{t}^{3}+\frac{5}{9}{t}^{2}-\frac{8}{9}t)|}_{1}^{x} \\  & =-\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\frac{8}{9}x-(-\frac{2}{27}+\frac{5}{9}-\frac{8}{9}) \\  & =-\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\frac{8}{9}x+\frac{11}{27}.\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\ -\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\frac{8}{9}x+\frac{11}{27}, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186442324 :question/id #uuid "990f1bb6-e595-59df-8c02-d323344bc3ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-210785" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da4529e7-604e-506b-adaa-ff85312c20f9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{-x^{2}+8x-7}{9}" :db/id 17592186442316}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186442316} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ff772f-b783-5f66-89ac-69df3d1d8f2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186442319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

$$
f(x)=\{\begin{aligned}-\frac{2}{9}x+\frac{8}{9},\, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 0,\, & \text{otherwise}\end{aligned}
$$

its cumulative distribution function is 

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0,\, & x<1 \\ h(x),\, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 1,\, & x>4\end{aligned}
$$

where $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $1\le x\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\ {\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4\end{aligned}
$$

For the given probability density function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t & ={\int }_{1}^{x}(-\frac{2}{9}t+\frac{8}{9})\,\text{d}t \\ \text{ } & ={(-\frac{1}{9}{t}^{2}+\frac{8}{9}t)|}_{1}^{x} \\  & =-\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}+\frac{8}{9}x-\frac{7}{9} \\  & =-\frac{1}{9}({x}^{2}-8x+7) \\  & =-\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7).\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\ -\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7), & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186442325 :question/id #uuid "e65ef0d7-6649-5f56-9e79-7407f7595f66" :question/math-academy-id "q-89621" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c66a62f-9a33-540e-bb1b-485e50f03db9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442303} {:answer/id #uuid "12f66496-4995-5d37-a001-943fa360d144" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{5{x}^{2}}{16}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{64}" :db/id 17592186442305} {:answer/id #uuid "5de59784-191d-59f0-ab4e-cb2aafa6fe90" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442309} {:answer/id #uuid "7295486c-b630-5ce0-8356-5ab47719adad" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442311} {:answer/id #uuid "af97dd8a-6b84-534d-9a5b-b7c3f09bac24" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442313}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186442309} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0e871fb-e944-567c-b4fe-9835a0a9327f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186442321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

$$
f(x)=\{\begin{aligned}\frac{1}{64}x(16-{x}^{2}),\, & 0\le x\le 4 \\ 0,\, & \text{otherwise}\end{aligned}
$$

its cumulative distribution function is 

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0,\, & x<0 \\ h(x),\, & 0\le x\le 4 \\ 1,\, & x>4.\end{aligned}
$$

Find the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability density function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0<x<4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\ {\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t, & 0\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4\end{aligned}
$$

For the given probability density function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t & ={\int }_{0}^{x}\frac{1}{64}t(16-{t}^{2})\,\text{d}t \\  & ={\frac{1}{64}(8{t}^{2}-\frac{{t}^{4}}{4})|}_{0}^{x} \\  & =\frac{1}{64}(8{x}^{2}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}) \\  & =\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}.\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\ \frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}, & 0\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186500304 :question/id #uuid "471d1d77-25cd-5101-acd9-2310f0d5d168" :question/math-academy-id "q-89672" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2dedee-a9a6-5f08-aaca-929e3c0e1a1e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-8x-16" :db/id 17592186499679} {:answer/id #uuid "215bd0d9-f220-5e68-82fa-30f7f2f20f6f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}+8x-15" :db/id 17592186499729} {:answer/id #uuid "6f65d4dc-2c09-5761-b57d-65243b8be70c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-8x-15" :db/id 17592186499863} {:answer/id #uuid "9697c8ec-2113-54d6-875d-643ae67cf997" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{-{x}^{2}+8x-15}{2}" :db/id 17592186499949} {:answer/id #uuid "ea81b801-f204-59da-86c8-5fb92620fdc7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-8x-30" :db/id 17592186500138}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186499729} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4dd9342-bbc6-5cbd-86b8-630a593c1561" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186500266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

$$
f(x)=\{\begin{aligned}2(-x+4),\, & 3\le x\le 4 \\ 0,\, & \text{otherwise}\end{aligned}
$$

its cumulative distribution function is 

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0,\, & x<3 \\ h(x),\, & 3\le x\le 4 \\ 1,\, & x>4.\end{aligned}
$$

Find the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $3\le x\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\ {\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t, & 3\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4\end{aligned}
$$

For the given probability density function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t & ={\int }_{3}^{x}2(-t+4)\,\text{d}t \\ \text{ } & ={8t-{t}^{2}|}_{3}^{x} \\  & =-{x}^{2}+8x-15.\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\ -{x}^{2}+8x-15, & 3\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186501183 :question/id #uuid "770dc96c-77d3-556b-b303-18d387043365" :question/math-academy-id "q-89606" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c522a9a-a340-5730-935a-e853421c44ca" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{75-2x}{75}" :db/id 17592186500525} {:answer/id #uuid "49f3c406-0b5e-5522-a240-414ac7e0f856" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{2}-25}{75}" :db/id 17592186500615} {:answer/id #uuid "887364d0-5dcf-5d1a-9cb5-af1322ef590e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{75-{x}^{2}}{75}" :db/id 17592186500754} {:answer/id #uuid "b55dc857-62d1-5ed0-85ee-8b7c291b0260" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{75}x" :db/id 17592186500845} {:answer/id #uuid "f364853a-396b-5d86-bdbe-5ffe621626d8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{75}{x}^{2}" :db/id 17592186500984}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186500615} :answer-field/id #uuid "94adf626-a400-5181-b287-7ccffcedb8aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186501085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

$$
f(x)=\{\begin{aligned}\frac{2}{75}x,\, & 5\le x\le 10 \\ 0,\, & \text{otherwise}\end{aligned}
$$

its cumulative distribution function is 

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0,\, & x<5 \\ h(x),\, & 5\le x\le 10 \\ 1,\, & x>10.\end{aligned}
$$

Find the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $5\le x\le 10,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<5 \\ {\int }_{5}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t, & 5\le x\le 10 \\ 1, & x>10\end{aligned}
$$

For the given probability density function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{5}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t & ={\int }_{5}^{x}\frac{2}{75}t\,\text{d}t \\ \text{ } & ={\frac{1}{75}{t}^{2}|}_{5}^{x} \\  & =\frac{1}{75}{x}^{2}-\frac{1}{3} \\  & =\frac{{x}^{2}-25}{75}.\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0,\, & x<5, \\ \frac{{x}^{2}-25}{75},\, & 5\le x\le 10, \\ 1,\, & x>10.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186133519 :question/id #uuid "707e3b49-9c13-50d8-8a7f-c4d5ec44e0ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-13365"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbc399b-90f3-5acd-ac70-7345a8436978" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186134539 :question/id #uuid "d416c744-adfb-5c13-80ec-0e124bb7f438" :question/math-academy-id "q-89139"} {:db/id 17592186134540 :question/id #uuid "dc0b739c-e444-5ab3-bcd2-409b731d56fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-89612"} {:db/id 17592186419944 :question/id #uuid "3191d215-7e03-5aae-a424-72356e84e8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-126177"} {:db/id 17592186419945 :question/id #uuid "3ffe741c-4355-5cb4-a113-2fae2e76fdee" :question/math-academy-id "q-89700"} {:db/id 17592186419946 :question/id #uuid "502fa5ed-8192-5239-85ce-b51fd4a6a69d" :question/math-academy-id "q-89747"} {:db/id 17592186419948 :question/id #uuid "83a3d348-6693-5dcc-af5c-61cd638a0bb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-89746"} {:db/id 17592186419957 :question/id #uuid "de421a60-85ed-5a5a-9a98-5df02c4cb3f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126176"} {:db/id 17592186424146 :question/id #uuid "a285feed-066b-52a2-a5c2-8c1c741cc3d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-89738"} {:db/id 17592186424147 :question/id #uuid "cbafb4bb-6bd6-540c-9367-06ab0b677b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-126178"} {:db/id 17592186424887 :question/id #uuid "5d72a8e6-eda0-59be-829b-e0298d5412e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-89695"} {:db/id 17592186442322 :question/id #uuid "365bf094-f659-5822-bf63-2e5a6992d995" :question/math-academy-id "q-89745"} {:db/id 17592186500293 :question/id #uuid "2175ed2b-85f5-5f4e-9b21-fd44965b957e" :question/math-academy-id "q-126173"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF"} {:db/id 17592186133519 :question/id #uuid "707e3b49-9c13-50d8-8a7f-c4d5ec44e0ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-13365"} {:db/id 17592186134539 :question/id #uuid "d416c744-adfb-5c13-80ec-0e124bb7f438" :question/math-academy-id "q-89139" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a96b44b4-1f7e-576d-9e77-9ec278a83d36" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{2}" :db/id 17592186133273} {:answer/id #uuid "107b6d59-d74b-5f3c-9bc5-01a9d06b20b7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{e}" :db/id 17592186133276} {:answer/id #uuid "105177ed-381e-5551-8d54-f794cc7ae2f7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/id 17592186442304} {:answer/id #uuid "c6834059-6614-531c-86f9-081bd2ed69b6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/id 17592186442314} {:answer/id #uuid "f7ff0cb6-5ee6-5486-95b5-ba7fabd16b87" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{1}{e}" :db/id 17592186442317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186442304} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3fece95-8a02-51e6-a7b8-03ddf8d52dc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186133272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\ 1-{e}^{-x}, & x\ge 0,\end{aligned}
$$

find $P(X>2).$" :question/worked-solution "We can perform this computation using the complement, as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\le 2) \\  & =1-F(2) \\  & =1-(1-{e}^{-2}) \\  & ={e}^{-2} \\  & =\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186134540 :question/id #uuid "dc0b739c-e444-5ab3-bcd2-409b731d56fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-89612" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f4af3cf-f231-595b-aaf4-49e10d20ff41" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{9}{25}" :db/id 17592186133280} {:answer/id #uuid "e6bd978c-da5d-59dd-85e1-a2c03295ee58" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{8}{25}" :db/id 17592186133281} {:answer/id #uuid "f256f7ab-c378-584b-ab95-d8f9f46921ca" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{4}{25}" :db/id 17592186133282} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3624d2-d1b2-5d89-8864-4bd4b45113e1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{8}{25}" :db/id 17592186500616} {:answer/id #uuid "c3226fc1-cbce-5f81-a7bd-59cad1dcc127" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+\frac{8}{25}" :db/id 17592186500875}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186133281} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2ed936f-3ea8-56c4-8eab-fb9925367eff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186133278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\ \frac{{x}^{2}}{25}, & 0\le x\le 5 \\ 1, & x>5,\end{aligned}
$$

find $P(1\le X\le 3).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform the computation as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}P(1\le X\le 3) & =P(1<X\le 3) \\  & =P(X\le 3)-P(X\le 1) \\  & =F(3)-F(1) \\  & =\frac{{3}^{2}}{25}-\frac{{1}^{2}}{25} \\  & =\frac{8}{25}\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186419944 :question/id #uuid "3191d215-7e03-5aae-a424-72356e84e8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-126177"} {:db/id 17592186419945 :question/id #uuid "3ffe741c-4355-5cb4-a113-2fae2e76fdee" :question/math-academy-id "q-89700"} {:db/id 17592186419946 :question/id #uuid "502fa5ed-8192-5239-85ce-b51fd4a6a69d" :question/math-academy-id "q-89747"} {:db/id 17592186419948 :question/id #uuid "83a3d348-6693-5dcc-af5c-61cd638a0bb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-89746"} {:db/id 17592186419957 :question/id #uuid "de421a60-85ed-5a5a-9a98-5df02c4cb3f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126176"} {:db/id 17592186424146 :question/id #uuid "a285feed-066b-52a2-a5c2-8c1c741cc3d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-89738"} {:db/id 17592186424147 :question/id #uuid "cbafb4bb-6bd6-540c-9367-06ab0b677b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-126178"} {:db/id 17592186424887 :question/id #uuid "5d72a8e6-eda0-59be-829b-e0298d5412e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-89695" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d43dadc-2415-595b-83bd-07293e62a4d7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{2}{5}" :db/id 17592186424868} {:answer/id #uuid "2d728c61-ee7a-5242-b976-dff68318b24a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{4}{5}" :db/id 17592186424870} {:answer/id #uuid "54302da3-4ffd-5ae6-9474-e5f95bb705f9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186424874} {:answer/id #uuid "86635ef4-b567-5842-a8be-7564b4bc47cb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{5}" :db/id 17592186424876} {:answer/id #uuid "c53339f9-decf-5456-b59e-339275bad539" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{3}{5}" :db/id 17592186424879}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186424870} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf2e7998-6dc3-5838-ae14-0d427c2b4449" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186424885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "Given that the 