Given that $\text{E}[X]=\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}},$ compute $\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X].$

*Hint: You may assume that $\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\text{E}[X]+b\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:

$$
\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X]=4\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\text{E}[X]
$$

For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by

$$
\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\cdot f(x)\,\text{d}x.
$$

We already know $\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\cdot f(x)\,\text{d}x \\  & ={\int }_{{e}^{-2}}^{1}{x}^{2}\cdot \frac{1}{2x}\,\text{d}x \\  & ={\int }_{{e}^{-2}}^{1}\frac{x}{2}\,\text{d}x \\  & ={\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\,|}_{{e}^{-2}}^{1} \\  & =\frac{1}{4}-\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}}\end{aligned}
$$

Substituting $\text{E}[X]=\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}$ and $\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\frac{1}{4}-\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that

$$
\begin{aligned}\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X] & =4\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\text{E}[X] \\  & =4(\frac{1}{4}-\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}})-2(\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}) \\  & =1-\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}-1+\frac{1}{{e}^{2}} \\  & =\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "1ec8cc12-b2a4-5daf-96fd-1e378052ed2d" :step/next {:db/id 17592186479152}} {:db/id 17592186479149 :step/content {:db/id 17592186479115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85e8f87d-a86b-5e5a-9b4c-520af1d67778" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{7}{2}" :db/id 17592186478767} {:answer/id #uuid "8a5de172-0879-5846-8775-50301538400b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186478775} {:answer/id #uuid "8c404e33-978f-5492-8afd-92388f08864c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{11}{8}" :db/id 17592186478781} {:answer/id #uuid "92a6058f-3718-55b4-83a2-afc873b42494" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{6}{5}" :db/id 17592186478797} {:answer/id #uuid "a7862d49-f18d-5362-98d3-095ce5b8964a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{13}{5}" :db/id 17592186478832}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186478832} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b35dd5-9730-5404-b881-f84b63c0e854" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186478998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ac78b028-e0aa-5c92-b54a-b1ba1527a82f" :question/math-academy-id "q-152915" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function 

