\begin{aligned}\text{E}[5X-3{X}^{2}] & =5\text{E}[X]-3\text{E}[{X}^{2}] \\  & =5\cdot 2-3\cdot \frac{13}{3} \\  & =10-13 \\  & =-3.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "b234828c-5807-5de4-a2a5-5f231ccf4ede" :step/next {:db/id 17592186508137}} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13ed44a6-241d-5838-9fc9-af9b6f83e61d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{3}{2}" :db/id 17592186507622} {:answer/id #uuid "1578c936-8ad1-508e-aa56-b4990c519451" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186507624} {:answer/id #uuid "67abf3a2-af43-5891-a4b8-887a1c46a81b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186507751} {:answer/id #uuid "7e517eaa-0474-52ae-938e-84dbfaa53de5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186507784} {:answer/id #uuid "8dda24db-7965-57a0-84c8-bf571ddd300c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{7}{3}" :db/id 17592186507800}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186507624} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5d3c470-c959-5590-9ddc-7ea57ee65776" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186508029} {:answer/id #uuid "13ed44a6-241d-5838-9fc9-af9b6f83e61d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{3}{2}" :db/id 17592186507622} {:answer/id #uuid "1578c936-8ad1-508e-aa56-b4990c519451" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186507624} {:answer/id #uuid "67abf3a2-af43-5891-a4b8-887a1c46a81b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186507751} {:answer/id #uuid "7e517eaa-0474-52ae-938e-84dbfaa53de5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186507784} {:answer/id #uuid "8dda24db-7965-57a0-84c8-bf571ddd300c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{7}{3}" :db/id 17592186507800} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b58a9e1-f2e5-5bab-86c3-1dc62a5bf1dc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186434407} {:answer/id #uuid "83994b5b-dec3-525b-9473-71abebd50a27" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186434408} {:answer/id #uuid "908f1924-a4cc-5cae-83ec-6a4c7872904f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186434410} {:answer/id #uuid "93d5d0a4-79ad-5a4d-854e-315f284a4eac" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186434411} {:answer/id #uuid "a25f9bac-857f-5e6a-8fee-76b7ccf2820e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186434412}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186434408} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c9c34c2-a686-5dff-8116-1e613117e2fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186434424} {:answer/id #uuid "7b58a9e1-f2e5-5bab-86c3-1dc62a5bf1dc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186434407} {:answer/id #uuid "83994b5b-dec3-525b-9473-71abebd50a27" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186434408} {:answer/id #uuid "908f1924-a4cc-5cae-83ec-6a4c7872904f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186434410} {:answer/id #uuid "93d5d0a4-79ad-5a4d-854e-315f284a4eac" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186434411} {:answer/id #uuid "a25f9bac-857f-5e6a-8fee-76b7ccf2820e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186434412} {:activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id 17592186130036} :activity/id #uuid "b93dfde4-f3d0-56f7-90c3-7b5628613c8b" :activity/scope {:db/id 17592186048800 :topic/id #uuid "c021e608-4c8b-5191-872f-f3e0b02d2d4a" :topic/math-academy-id 1983} :activity/steps [{:db/id 17592186130035 :step/content {:db/id 17592186129173 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186128992 :question/id #uuid "e17f982d-3d3e-5279-b507-d390e4f1970f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6116"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048820}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186129850} {:db/id 17592186129851} {:db/id 17592186339104} {:db/id 17592186339105} {:db/id 17592186339106} {:db/id 17592186339108} {:db/id 17592186365115} {:db/id 17592186366240} {:db/id 17592186366247} {:db/id 17592186366254}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"} :step/id #uuid "ac75c745-5dbd-5824-9f7d-04a8faf6a86c" :step/math-academy-id 22705 :step/next {:db/id 17592186130037}} {:db/id 17592186130036 :step/content {:db/id 17592186130377 :tutorial/content "Recall that we use **sigma notation** to write sums concisely. For example, 

$$
\displaystyle \sum_{i=1}^n a_i
$$

refers to the sum of all terms in the sequence $a_i,$ where the **index** $i$ ranges from $1$ to $n\mathbin{:}$

$$
\sum_{i=1}^n a_i = a_1+a_2+\cdots+a_n
$$

Sigma notation can also represent sums whose terms depend on two indices. That is, **double sums** of the form 

$$
\displaystyle \sum_{i=1}^m \sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij}
$$


where $i$ ranges from $1$ to $m,$ and $j$ ranges from $1$ to $n\mathbin.$ Thus, a double summation is just a "sum of a sum." 

In calculating double summations, we follow two steps:

- First, we evaluate the inner sum by fixing the index of the outer sum ($i$) and incrementing only the inner index ($j$).

- Next, we evaluate the outer sum by incrementing the outer sum index.

To illustrate how it works, suppose we are given the following double sum:

$$
\sum_{i=1}^2 \sum_{j=1}^4 (i+j)
$$



To compute this double sum, we can proceed as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\sum }_{j=1}^{4}(i+j) & ={\sum }_{i=1}^{2}[({\sum }_{j=1}^{4}(i+j))] \\  & ={\sum }_{i=1}^{2}[(i+1)+(i+2)+(i+3)+(i+4)] \\  & ={\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(4i+10) \\  & =4(1)+10+4(2)+10 \\  & =4+10+8+10 \\  & =32\end{aligned}
$$

Later, we will provide some formulas that will help us simplify many double summations calculations." :tutorial/id #uuid "3c842b98-cbdf-55a4-96a1-360697763430" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3867 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "583e493e-9206-508f-b782-7eec0883a7d5" :step/math-academy-id 22707 :step/next {:db/id 17592186130035}} {:db/id 17592186130037 :step/content {:db/id 17592186130378 :tutorial/content "Double summations satisfy the following properties:

**The Constant Multiple Rule** 

We can factor out a constant multiple from a double summation:

$$
\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^m\sum_{j=1}^n k a_{ij} = k\sum_{i=1}^m\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij}
$$

**The Sum Rule** 

We can distribute a double summation over a sum of terms.

$$
\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^m\sum_{j=1}^n (a_{ij} + b_{ij}) = \sum_{i=1}^m\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij} + \sum_{i=1}^m\sum_{j=1}^n b_{ij}
$$

**The Double Sum of Units**

Recall that for single summations, we have

$$
\sum_{j=1}^{n} 1 = \underbrace{1+1+\cdots+1}_{n\textrm{ times}}  = n.
$$

Analogously for double summations, we have that

$$
\sum_{i=1}^m\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn.
$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "41df0fcf-551a-58a5-b47e-ac1ddd121f7f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3868 :tutorial/title "The Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"} :step/id #uuid "3d0a00d2-9ccc-5261-bfa0-15e1bf5cb3c6" :step/math-academy-id 22708 :step/next {:db/id 17592186130038}} {:db/id 17592186130038 :step/content {:db/id 17592186129174 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186128993 :question/id #uuid "e8f3608f-68f2-5ba9-b618-447887e7f6fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-6118"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048922}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186129499} {:db/id 17592186129500} {:db/id 17592186275222} {:db/id 17592186275223} {:db/id 17592186275224} {:db/id 17592186275225} {:db/id 17592186275226} {:db/id 17592186275227} {:db/id 17592186275228} {:db/id 17592186363356} {:db/id 17592186365122}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"} :step/id #uuid "42e12d98-e4bf-512d-b3c2-5c93584fc740" :step/math-academy-id 22710 :step/next {:db/id 17592186130196}} {:db/id 17592186130195 :step/content {:db/id 17592186129259 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186128835 :question/id #uuid "d180f745-028b-5859-8cad-4a49b5c20773" :question/math-academy-id "e-10521"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186129501} {:db/id 17592186129502} {:db/id 17592186275229} {:db/id 17592186275234} {:db/id 17592186275237} {:db/id 17592186275239} {:db/id 17592186275241} {:db/id 17592186275242} {:db/id 17592186365129} {:db/id 17592186365136} {:db/id 17592186365143} {:db/id 17592186371865}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"} :step/id #uuid "4e8c00d9-bc34-56d4-a71a-61e0e176e8fb" :step/math-academy-id 39727} {:db/id 17592186130196 :step/content {:db/id 17592186130453 :tutorial/content "In addition, we have the following useful rules:

