$$

For the given probability density function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t & ={\int }_{0}^{x}\frac{1}{64}t(16-{t}^{2})\,\text{d}t \\  & ={\frac{1}{64}(8{t}^{2}-\frac{{t}^{4}}{4})|}_{0}^{x} \\  & =\frac{1}{64}(8{x}^{2}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}) \\  & =\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}.\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\ \frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}, & 0\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "443e51e5-e403-51ae-bbff-e563149f49e5" :step/next {:db/id 17592186442326}} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c66a62f-9a33-540e-bb1b-485e50f03db9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442303} {:answer/id #uuid "12f66496-4995-5d37-a001-943fa360d144" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{5{x}^{2}}{16}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{64}" :db/id 17592186442305} {:answer/id #uuid "5de59784-191d-59f0-ab4e-cb2aafa6fe90" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442309} {:answer/id #uuid "7295486c-b630-5ce0-8356-5ab47719adad" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442311} {:answer/id #uuid "af97dd8a-6b84-534d-9a5b-b7c3f09bac24" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442313}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186442309} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0e871fb-e944-567c-b4fe-9835a0a9327f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186442321} {:answer/id #uuid "0c66a62f-9a33-540e-bb1b-485e50f03db9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442303} {:answer/id #uuid "12f66496-4995-5d37-a001-943fa360d144" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{5{x}^{2}}{16}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{64}" :db/id 17592186442305} {:answer/id #uuid "5de59784-191d-59f0-ab4e-cb2aafa6fe90" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442309} {:answer/id #uuid "7295486c-b630-5ce0-8356-5ab47719adad" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442311} {:answer/id #uuid "af97dd8a-6b84-534d-9a5b-b7c3f09bac24" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/id 17592186442313} {:db/id 17592186442328 :step/content {:db/id 17592186442324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da4529e7-604e-506b-adaa-ff85312c20f9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{-x^{2}+8x-7}{9}" :db/id 17592186442316}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186442316} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ff772f-b783-5f66-89ac-69df3d1d8f2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186442319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "990f1bb6-e595-59df-8c02-d323344bc3ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-210785" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

$$
f(x)=\{\begin{aligned}-\frac{2}{9}x+\frac{8}{9},\, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 0,\, & \text{otherwise}\end{aligned}
$$

its cumulative distribution function is 

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0,\, & x<1 \\ h(x),\, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 1,\, & x>4\end{aligned}
$$

where $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $1\le x\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\ {\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t, & 1\le x\le 4 \\ 1, & x>4\end{aligned}
$$

For the given probability density function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t & ={\int }_{1}^{x}(-\frac{2}{9}t+\frac{8}{9})\,\text{d}t \\ \text{ } & ={(-\frac{1}{9}{t}^{2}+\frac{8}{9}t)|}_{1}^{x} \\  & =-\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}+\frac{8}{9}x-\frac{7}{9} \\  & =-\frac{1}{9}({x}^{2}-8x+7) \\  & =-\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7).\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

