$$"} :step/id #uuid "39d0ba9a-b08d-5b45-b5bf-8a3943de2319" :step/next {:db/id 17592186501259}} {:db/id 17592186501283 :step/content {:db/id 17592186501225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b593b2a-af8d-5c4e-9746-8d5e8f4120fb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\frac{e^{-x}}{2}" :db/id 17592186500523}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186500523} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb588555-9fd1-5660-8555-bc1960f97262" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492} :db/id 17592186501104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d0e0e171-2942-5666-9f4c-984a9e7d868a" :question/math-academy-id "q-185531" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

$$
f(x)=\frac{{e}^{-|x|}}{2},\,x\in (-\infty ,\infty ),
$$

its cumulative distribution function is

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}\frac{{e}^{x}}{2},\, & x\le 0 \\ h(x),\, & x>0\end{aligned}
$$

where $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)=\{\begin{aligned}{\int }_{-\infty }^{x}\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\,\text{d}t, & x<0 \\ {\int }_{-\infty }^{0}\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\,\text{d}t+{\int }_{0}^{x}\frac{{e}^{-t}}{2}\,\text{d}t, & x\ge 0\end{aligned}
$$

Let's compute the integrals.

- If $x\le 0,$ we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{-\infty }^{x}\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\,\text{d}t & ={\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}|}_{-\infty }^{x} \\  & =\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}.\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{-\infty }^{0}\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\,\text{d}t & ={\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\  & =\frac{1}{2}.\end{aligned}
$$

- If $x>0,$ we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{0}^{x}\frac{{e}^{-t}}{2}\,\text{d}t & =-{\frac{{e}^{-t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\  & =-\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}+\frac{1}{2}.\end{aligned}
$$

As a result, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{-\infty }^{0}\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\,\text{d}t+{\int }_{0}^{x}\frac{{e}^{-t}}{2}\,\text{d}t & =\frac{1}{2}+(-\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}+\frac{1}{2}) \\  & =1-\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}.\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}\frac{{e}^{x}}{2},\, & x\le 0 \\ 1-\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2},\, & x>0.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "b33ab878-bbe3-5d53-9e65-806860542c47"}] :activity/title "Cumulative Distribution Functions for Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id 17592186500457} {:db/id 17592186501258 :step/content {:db/id 17592186501183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c522a9a-a340-5730-935a-e853421c44ca" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{75-2x}{75}" :db/id 17592186500525} {:answer/id #uuid "49f3c406-0b5e-5522-a240-414ac7e0f856" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{2}-25}{75}" :db/id 17592186500615} {:answer/id #uuid "887364d0-5dcf-5d1a-9cb5-af1322ef590e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{75-{x}^{2}}{75}" :db/id 17592186500754} {:answer/id #uuid "b55dc857-62d1-5ed0-85ee-8b7c291b0260" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{75}x" :db/id 17592186500845} {:answer/id #uuid "f364853a-396b-5d86-bdbe-5ffe621626d8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{75}{x}^{2}" :db/id 17592186500984}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186500615} :answer-field/id #uuid "94adf626-a400-5181-b287-7ccffcedb8aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186501085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "770dc96c-77d3-556b-b303-18d387043365" :question/math-academy-id "q-89606" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function

