$$

Find the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $5\le x\le 10,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:

$$
F(x)=P(X\le x)=\{\begin{aligned}0, & x<5 \\ {\int }_{5}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t, & 5\le x\le 10 \\ 1, & x>10\end{aligned}
$$

For the given probability density function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{5}^{x}f(t)\,\text{d}t & ={\int }_{5}^{x}\frac{2}{75}t\,\text{d}t \\ \text{ } & ={\frac{1}{75}{t}^{2}|}_{5}^{x} \\  & =\frac{1}{75}{x}^{2}-\frac{1}{3} \\  & =\frac{{x}^{2}-25}{75}.\end{aligned}
$$

So, the cumulative distribution function is given by

$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}0,\, & x<5, \\ \frac{{x}^{2}-25}{75},\, & 5\le x\le 10, \\ 1,\, & x>10.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "242c6578-3fc8-593e-975a-c9f65e32ad15" :step/next {:db/id 17592186501263}} {:db/id 17592186501252 :step/content {:db/id 17592186500293 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e338a7c-f5c5-55b6-800b-47f10296b1d7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{112}{729}" :db/id 17592186499686} {:answer/id #uuid "4673f4bc-028d-52bd-b6cb-43a313197f90" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{23}{1458}" :db/id 17592186499785} {:answer/id #uuid "60d5eb82-e934-5a50-abfb-6bb988e212e5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{230}{729}" :db/id 17592186499844} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8b3642-18a5-59b9-ba90-c44b1dc2ff93" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{130}{729}" :db/id 17592186499989} {:answer/id #uuid "b05849a6-fd14-5761-ac6a-f3df6f46c897" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{113}{1458}" :db/id 17592186500007}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186499844} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecc71117-bad7-5cf6-bbde-8b45ac8873de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186500274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2175ed2b-85f5-5f4e-9b21-fd44965b957e" :question/math-academy-id "q-126173" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function

$$
