the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by

$$
f(x,y)=1+ax-y+{x}^{2}+bxy+c{y}^{2}.
$$

Find the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "If the function $f(x,y)$ is twice differentiable at $(x,y)=(0,0),$ then the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈\overset{\text{Linear approximation}}{\overset{⏞}{f(0,0)+{f}_{x}(0,0)\cdot x+{f}_{y}(0,0)\cdot y}} \\  & \,\,+{{\frac{1}{2}({f}_{xx}(0,0)\cdot {x}^{2}+2{f}_{xy}(0,0)\cdot xy+{f}_{yy}(0,0)\cdot {y}^{2})}_{⏟}}_{\text{Quadratic part}}.\end{aligned}
$$

Now, we compute the terms of our Taylor polynomial.

- Calculating the value of the function, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}f(0,0) & =1.\end{aligned}
$$

- Calculating the first derivatives, we have the following:

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =-\frac{1}{(x+y+1)^{2}}, & \,{f}_{y}(x,y) & =-\frac{1}{(x+y+1)^{2}} \\ {f}_{x}(0,0) & =-1, & \,{f}_{y}(0,0) & =-1\end{aligned}
$$

- Calculating the second derivatives, we have the following:

$$
\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =\frac{2}{(x+y+1)^{3}}, & \,{f}_{xx}(0,0) & =2 \\ {f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\frac{2}{(x+y+1)^{3}}, & \,{f}_{xy}(0,0) & =2 \\ {f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\frac{2}{(x+y+1)^{3}}, & \,{f}_{yy}(0,0) & =2\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈1+(-1)\cdot x+(-1)\cdot y+\frac{1}{2}(2\cdot {x}^{2}+2(2)\cdot xy+2\cdot {y}^{2}) \\  & =1+(-1)x-y+{x}^{2}+2xy+1{y}^{2}.\end{aligned}
$$

Finally,

$$
a+b+c=-1+2+1=2.
$$"} {:db/id 17592186198435 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186198077 :question/id #uuid "1d13a6c0-0912-5089-81ed-c298bf747ccd" :question/math-academy-id "e-12563"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b91ae708-a63d-51ac-9ae0-f24724392858" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048859}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186198637 :question/id #uuid "6d7c182a-d8d9-5d67-83bd-5c70deb44da7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162947"} {:db/id 17592186198643 :question/id #uuid "2ec5ff3d-fd4d-5171-8304-f2a9e9fbb4f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-162989"} {:db/id 17592186281602 :question/id #uuid "c7c75fe7-9dcd-544f-9c7d-b36cf94f46b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163102"} {:db/id 17592186281603 :question/id #uuid "b07db089-383d-5673-822f-6a5d7846d04c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163104"} {:db/id 17592186281607 :question/id #uuid "e7670cca-4082-532e-925a-af41e094c0c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-163122"} {:db/id 17592186281608 :question/id #uuid "2c3dba84-c7b2-5a37-bb07-b58c80773105" :question/math-academy-id "q-163142"} {:db/id 17592186281609 :question/id #uuid "f0b608b5-0740-5c5c-a8d8-286478d0cfd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-163143"} {:db/id 17592186281610 :question/id #uuid "61a1651c-7c64-5ebe-93b5-ec0cfeb0b0a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163144"} {:db/id 17592186367811 :question/id #uuid "cdc26b29-0619-5b64-aa82-450f2b706603" :question/math-academy-id "q-163106"} {:db/id 17592186367825 :question/id #uuid "45c5b66d-4dfc-59b3-9af3-6cbfa7931243" :question/math-academy-id "q-163123"} {:db/id 17592186432372 :question/id #uuid "c474ae22-f722-549c-93e7-7a344f22e1ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-163127"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Taylor Polynomial in Matrix Form"} {:db/id 17592186198077 :question/id #uuid "1d13a6c0-0912-5089-81ed-c298bf747ccd" :question/math-academy-id "e-12563" :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id 17592186198435 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b91ae708-a63d-51ac-9ae0-f24724392858" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a 