Use the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $a=\begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 1 \\ 1\end{bmatrix}$ to approximate the value of $f(0,2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that the function $f:{R}^{n}\to R$ is defined by 

$$
f:\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ ⋮ \\ {x}_{n}\end{bmatrix}⟶z
$$



and is twice differentiable at $x=a.$ Then, the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $a$ is given by

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x) & ≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}{f}^{″}(a)(x-a),\end{aligned}
$$

where

$$
{f}^{′}(a)={\begin{bmatrix}\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\end{bmatrix}|}_{x=a}
$$

and

$$
{f}^{″}(a)={\begin{bmatrix}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\ \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\end{bmatrix}}_{x=a}
$$

In this case, we have $a=\begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 1 \\ 1\end{bmatrix},$ and the following data:

$$
\begin{aligned}f(a) & =-1, & \,{f}^{′}(a) & =\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2\end{bmatrix}, & \,{f}^{″}(a) & =\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\ -1 & 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by

$$
f(x)≈-1+\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}x-1 \\ y-1 \\ z-1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{2}{\begin{bmatrix}x-1 \\ y-1 \\ z-1\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\ -1 & 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}x-1 \\ y-1 \\ z-1\end{bmatrix}
$$

Finally, evaluating the polynomial at $x=\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 2 \\ 0\end{bmatrix},$ we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}f(0,2,0) & ≈-1+\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}0-1 \\ 2-1 \\ 0-1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{2}{\begin{bmatrix}0-1 \\ 2-1 \\ 0-1\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\ -1 & 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}0-1 \\ 2-1 \\ 0-1\end{bmatrix} \\  & =-1+\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\ 1 \\ -1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{2}{\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\ 1 \\ -1\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\ -1 & 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\ 1 \\ -1\end{bmatrix} \\  & =-1+(-4)+\frac{1}{2}\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ -2 \\ 2\end{bmatrix} \\  & =-5+\frac{1}{2}(-6) \\  & =-8.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186367901 :question/id #uuid "34533486-cd0d-5205-b2b8-1ba449843c04" :question/math-academy-id "q-164861"} {:db/id 17592186367908 :question/id #uuid "a2bdcbd2-3eb2-5c14-bb14-2f06b27bbd7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-164862"} {:db/id 17592186432371 :question/id #uuid "86a1a7c8-4805-516c-8e49-de078c8ddcd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-164829" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186198436 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19cc766-bdc5-5ab2-aa4d-ebddf8311116" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating a Multivariable Function at a Point Using a Quadratic Taylor Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193ecd87-052b-5366-b53d-f4fee3109be5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186432340} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc4ca25-f9ab-58f2-a71f-3c12f6fe8a62" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id 17592186432347} {:answer/id #uuid "7820c9d8-f18b-54a7-b0f6-12cdd2dda51a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\frac{9}{2}" :db/id 17592186432350} {:answer/id #uuid "9df1526a-c9df-5b82-9e9f-cdc5b44e9599" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{5}{2}" :db/id 17592186432353} {:answer/id #uuid "e7cc9897-e991-5a5c-9fd2-252b1cef639e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186432360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "193ecd87-052b-5366-b53d-f4fee3109be5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186432340} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb6cb031-bae3-5718-a823-8bb4cf052480" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186432368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "For the twice-differentiable function $f:{R}^{2}\to R,$ we have the following data:

