Calculate ${\int }_{C}\,\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={cos}^{3}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3})$ for $0\le \theta \le \frac{3\pi }{2},$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,

$$
{\int }_{C}\,\text{d}s=L.
$$

In polar coordinates, the arc length element $\text{d}s$ is given by

$$
\text{d}s=\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\frac{\text{d}r}{\text{d}\theta })}^{2}}\,\text{d}\theta .
$$

So, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\theta )$ for ${\theta }_{1}\le \theta \le {\theta }_{2},$ we have

$$
L={\int }_{C}\,\text{d}s={\int }_{{\theta }_{1}}^{{\theta }_{2}}\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\frac{\text{d}r}{\text{d}\theta })}^{2}}\,\text{d}\theta .
$$

Since $r={cos}^{3}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3}),$ we have

$$
\frac{\text{d}r}{\text{d}\theta }=-\operatorname{sin}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3}){cos}^{2}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3}).
$$

Therefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{\int }_{C}\,\text{d}s & ={\int }_{{\theta }_{1}}^{{\theta }_{2}}\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\frac{\text{d}r}{\text{d}\theta })}^{2}}\,\text{d}\theta  \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{3\pi /2}\sqrt{{({cos}^{3}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3}))}^{2}+{(-\operatorname{sin}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3}){cos}^{2}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3}))}^{2}}\,\text{d}\theta  \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{3\pi /2}\sqrt{{cos}^{6}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3}){cos}^{4}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3})}\,\text{d}\theta  \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{3\pi /2}\sqrt{{cos}^{4}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3})[{cos}^{2}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3})]}\,\text{d}\theta  \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{3\pi /2}\sqrt{{cos}^{4}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3})}\,\text{d}\theta  \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{3\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡(\frac{\theta }{3})\text{d}\theta  \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{3\pi /2}\frac{1}{2}[1+\operatorname{cos}⁡(\frac{2\theta }{3})]\text{d}\theta  \\  & =\frac{1}{2}{[\theta +\frac{3}{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡(\frac{2\theta }{3})]}_{0}^{3\pi /2} \\  & =\frac{3\pi }{4}.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "73aaaa88-a71a-530e-8d01-e165dd7e3bfc"} {:db/id 17592186483473 :step/content {:db/id 17592186483373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "500ad374-633d-5acc-8fc6-2c954b7ceee0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{3\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id 17592186482954} {:answer/id #uuid "7daf2602-5ddf-5b93-9c8f-85bf86b1183f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186483033} {:answer/id #uuid "c4195c77-54de-55db-b8bc-7aa9584420e9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186483138} {:answer/id #uuid "dd638516-5b00-5d2e-b7d7-70996ad3e87f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{5\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id 17592186483185} {:answer/id #uuid "eb789a46-0304-547b-8796-b1b162722c73" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186483207}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186483033} :answer-field/id #uuid "416c49b7-a3b7-5531-9507-24f1c4541b91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186483261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6017b841-30bb-5249-81e7-cac41367e88a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123548" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b9ea317575efcb32d8234309e80fecfd4385c99dbe69dd9c33d3fa7d80313bb6.png)

