In the work that follows, we will only consider cases where $\det\left(\boldsymbol f''(\mathbf a)\right) \neq 0.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3cedcd0c-77c7-5789-b76d-7ae3307c237b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4263 :tutorial/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Taylor Polynomials"} {:db/id 17592186125645 :step/content {:db/id 17592186125885 :tutorial/content "To summarize, the point $\mathbf{a} \in \mathbb{R}^n$ is a stationary point of the function $f : \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}$ if $\boldsymbol{f}'(\mathbf{a}) = \mathbf 0^T,$ and we can classify $\mathbf{a}$ as follows:

