Let $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as
$r(t) = ⟨e^{\cos t}, e^{\sin t}⟩$ for $t ∈ [0, 2π]$. The area of $D$ can be written as

$Area(D) = ∬_(D)(\frac{∂Q}{∂x} - \frac{∂P}{∂y})dA = \displaystyle \int_{0}^{2π}AAAAAAAdt$,

