Let $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as
$r(t)=⟨\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\,\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩$ for $t\in [\frac{\pi }{3},\frac{5\pi }{3}].$ The area of $D$ can be written as

$$
\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\int }_{\pi /3}^{5\pi /3}\boxed{}\,dt,
$$

where $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$ Determine the missing part of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  

$$
\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.
$$

So, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\text{d}A \\  & ={∬}_{D}(\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y})\text{d}A \\  & ={∮}_{C}P\,\text{d}x+Q\,\text{d}y\end{aligned}
$$



Substituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get

$$
{∮}_{C}P\,\text{d}x+Q\,\text{d}y={∮}_{C}-y\,\text{d}x.
$$



The derivative of $r(t)$ is

$$
{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\,\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩.
$$

Therefore, we can write our line integral as

$$
\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}-y\,dx & ={\int }_{\pi /3}^{5\pi /3}-(\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\cdot (-\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\,dt \\  & ={\int }_{\pi /3}^{5\pi /3}(\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)(\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\,dt.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186442250 :question/id #uuid "30739161-7e72-5e37-b131-9975b77440f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-42315" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f00612-ca24-58a9-9a99-5bc9dff70695" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{sin}^{3}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442225} {:answer/id #uuid "244e3377-d03b-59bc-9a15-821691749cc3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{sin}^{4}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442228} {:answer/id #uuid "3b19e5e7-17b2-5ecd-8bda-2f5d049ec56f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{4}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442230} {:answer/id #uuid "4ac2fdfe-d325-50d4-8f82-69274f9797ee" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{sin}^{3}⁡t{cos}^{4}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442231} {:answer/id #uuid "4c93679f-96a9-5546-b831-28f2a59ed0bd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{sin}^{3}⁡t{cos}^{3}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442232}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186442228} :answer-field/id #uuid "1007d99f-4a44-5eca-8672-e3953d3b25aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186442245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "![](images/bf/bfec7cbdb26a3db773ab1f6207de436ff0856b331cda183da530dbb6b91d91bd.png)

Let $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as
$r(t)=⟨{cos}^{3}⁡t,\,{sin}^{3}⁡t⟩$ for $t\in [0,2\pi ].$ The area of $D$ can be written as

$$
\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\int }_{0}^{2\pi }\boxed{}\,dt,
$$

where $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$ Determine the missing part of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Our simple, piecewise-smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  

$$
\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.
$$

So, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\text{d}A \\  & ={∬}_{D}(\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y})\text{d}A \\  & ={∮}_{C}P\,\text{d}x+Q\,\text{d}y\end{aligned}
$$



Substituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get

$$
{∮}_{C}P\,\text{d}x+Q\,\text{d}y={∮}_{C}-y\,\text{d}x.
$$



The derivative of $r(t)$ is

$$
{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-3{cos}^{2}⁡t\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\,3{sin}^{2}⁡t\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.
$$

Therefore, we can write our line integral as

$$
\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}-y\,dx & ={\int }_{0}^{2\pi }(-{sin}^{3}⁡t)\cdot (-3{cos}^{2}⁡t\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\,dt \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{2\pi }3{sin}^{4}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\,dt.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186442252 :question/id #uuid "6653118e-2998-5812-b728-f3217528d405" :question/math-academy-id "q-126746" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14451dd1-51ba-5cb4-a62a-0a5d4ff055bf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "9{sin}^{2}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442227} {:answer/id #uuid "6f80c7b4-33fd-57db-876b-025e20021ccd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "9{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442235} {:answer/id #uuid "81dd9c9a-88ed-5edc-bb4a-ab112606e4e5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-9\operatorname{sin}⁡t\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442236} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4d50f5-796c-5fc2-a622-14130e42fc0e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\operatorname{sin}⁡t\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442241} {:answer/id #uuid "e911610a-7c47-5303-9138-bd0e5e56ae76" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-9{sin}^{2}⁡t" :db/id 17592186442244}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186442235} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5a72b7a-4d2b-5cb1-bfa9-dcf075591732" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186442248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "![](images/0a/0a60729b626e1e9e219a839898cacc18aa81ec2a9b1b445e7b92b721874c2550.png)

Let $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as
$r(t)=⟨3\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\,3\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $t\in [0,2\pi ].$ The area of $D$ can be written as

$$
\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\int }_{0}^{2\pi }\boxed{}\,dt,
$$

where $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ Determine the missing part of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  

$$
\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.
$$

So, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\text{d}A \\  & ={∬}_{D}(\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y})\text{d}A \\  & ={∮}_{C}P\,\text{d}x+Q\,\text{d}y\end{aligned}
$$



Substituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get

$$
{∮}_{C}P\,\text{d}x+Q\,\text{d}y={∮}_{C}x\,\text{d}y.
$$



The derivative of $r(t)$ is

$$
{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-3\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\,3\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.
$$

Therefore, we can write our line integral as

$$
\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x\,dy & ={\int }_{0}^{2\pi }3\operatorname{cos}⁡t\cdot 3\operatorname{cos}⁡t\,dt \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{2\pi }9{cos}^{2}⁡t\,dt.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186133897 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186133713 :question/id #uuid "aa4400ff-09b0-596c-9857-c13881b72f73" :question/math-academy-id "e-9555"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf9b73fa-c7ce-5c93-9131-ec36d29d6c3a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186134376 :question/id #uuid "3c3df1fb-6ba7-5d92-9c02-3f4fe719a847" :question/math-academy-id "q-42215"} {:db/id 17592186134386 :question/id #uuid "c299dba6-b9c4-559b-b05a-803d3465ef0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42298"} {:db/id 17592186369399 :question/id #uuid "8c42efa1-14e8-5edb-ba70-51dc3c6ff4b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-126722"} {:db/id 17592186369406 :question/id #uuid "5e16fd42-acd5-59dc-b36e-e5d23e861950" :question/math-academy-id "q-126725"} {:db/id 17592186369427 :question/id #uuid "8b773c29-9e6f-5096-b07b-de5aaca35eab" :question/math-academy-id "q-126818"} {:db/id 17592186369448 :question/id #uuid "7834afec-6e2d-5917-b360-ab0e90141806" :question/math-academy-id "q-126858"} {:db/id 17592186431051 :question/id #uuid "819104c2-11eb-5b49-9398-d7d5879660f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-126727"} {:db/id 17592186431052 :question/id #uuid "bd34f4a5-5a97-5165-88b5-594ad30569e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-126859"} {:db/id 17592186442251 :question/id #uuid "55130439-a2e5-560a-bbed-4ce47334253d" :question/math-academy-id "q-126757"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Area Using Green's Theorem"} {:db/id 17592186133713 :question/id #uuid "aa4400ff-09b0-596c-9857-c13881b72f73" :question/math-academy-id "e-9555"} {:db/id 17592186134376 :question/id #uuid "3c3df1fb-6ba7-5d92-9c02-3f4fe719a847" :question/math-academy-id "q-42215"} {:db/id 17592186134386 :question/id #uuid "c299dba6-b9c4-559b-b05a-803d3465ef0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42298" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86f48c0b-2a3d-5163-b8e8-0c7233eb05fb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{8}{5}" :db/id 17592186132356} {:answer/id #uuid "e01d132b-6218-5a49-8b31-