- ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}\,i-{t}^{3}\,j$ for $t\in [-1,1],$ and

- ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=2\,i+t\,j$ for $t\in [-1,1].$

Use Green's theorem to find the area of the region." :question/worked-solution "First, let $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$

Our simple, piecewise-smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented and  

$$
\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.
$$

So, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\text{d}A \\  & ={∬}_{D}(\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\frac{∂P}{∂y})\text{d}A \\  & ={∮}_{C}P\,\text{d}x+Q\,\text{d}y\end{aligned}
$$



Substituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get

$$
{∮}_{C}P\,\text{d}x+Q\,\text{d}y=-{∮}_{C}y\,\text{d}x.
$$



The derivatives of ${r}_{1}(t)$ and ${r}_{2}(t)$ are as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\, & {r}_{1}^{′}(t)=4t\,i-3{t}^{2}\,j \\ {C}_{2}:\, & {r}_{2}^{′}(t)=j\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, we can write our line integral as

$$
\begin{aligned}-{∮}_{C}y\,\text{d}x & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}\cup {C}_{2}}y\,dx \\  & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}y\,dx-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}y\,dx \\  & =-{\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{t}^{3})\cdot 4t\,\text{d}t-{\int }_{-1}^{1}t\cdot 0\,\text{d}t \\  & =4{\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{4}\,\text{d}t-0 \\  & =4[\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}]_{-1}^{1} \\  & =4\cdot \frac{2}{5} \\  & =\frac{8}{5}.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "3efe2d38-47eb-5856-81a2-431378bd1194" :step/next {:db/id 17592186442253}} {:db/id 17592186442253 :step/content {:db/id 17592186442249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "536ba388-fdb8-58ea-b126-38fbd2dcdb6b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)(\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)" :db/id 17592186442233} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f93b2c-abf4-5cbd-aa5b-d281bc9dc445" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)" :db/id 17592186442239} {:answer/id #uuid "ba5cc6be-612b-5620-9ea1-537324d438b6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)" :db/id 17592186442240} {:answer/id #uuid "c3dbd51c-9d36-5509-bb8b-877222cbaef9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)(\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)" :db/id 17592186442242} {:answer/id #uuid "de993e24-618b-5743-81ef-393206c8a109" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "(\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)(\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)" :db/id 17592186442243}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186442243} :answer-field/id #uuid "53872032-3b68-54a9-b047-b5722ee1ce8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186442246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "19d2b758-b269-5c92-aaaf-707449daf876" :question/math-academy-id "q-42301" :question/problem "![](images/ac/ac9f6016ee4c93aec58f8fff0a8002057f89d7c1bae589e5357a25709ae5a76c.png)

