</table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then

- $Σ$ is a $3\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,

- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\times 3$ matrix,

- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\times 2$ matrix.

From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\sigma }_{1}=5$ and ${\sigma }_{2}=0.$
Also, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$

Therefore, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\frac{1}{{\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\  & =\frac{1}{5}\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\ -2 & 4 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\frac{1}{5}\begin{bmatrix}-\sqrt{5} \\ 2\sqrt{5} \\ 0\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} \\ 0\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Since the second singular value is ${\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find vectors 

$$
u=\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ {x}_{3}\end{bmatrix}
$$

such that ${u}_{1}\cdot u=0$ and $‖u‖=1.$

Solving ${u}_{1}\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to

$$
-\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}{x}_{2}=0\,⟹\,-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0,
$$

we get the general solution 

$$
\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\ {x}_{2} \\ {x}_{3}\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}{{\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ 1 \\ 0\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{3}{{\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 0 \\ 1\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}},
$$

where ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables.

Notice that the two linearly independent solutions ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ are mutually orthogonal. Therefore, we only need to normalize them. This gives the second and third columns of $U:$   

$$
{u}_{2}=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ 0\end{bmatrix}\,{u}_{3}=\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 0 \\ 1\end{bmatrix}
$$

So, the matrix $U$ could be the following:

$$
U=\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} & \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} & \frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186423863 :question/id #uuid "bd607d3f-88f1-5057-a261-73a39b9023d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-363834"} {:db/id 17592186430360 :question/id #uuid "2cc63714-8ef0-5462-b695-51b69677adfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-363835" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "457a3842-15d8-5552-b245-a07a1675cac2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}_{3}" :db/id 17592186430278} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd9661f-8ecd-52f0-bb59-99f0d617f957" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186430285} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf668ec-1209-510a-bec2-b439f7a0fc64" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{3}" :db/id 17592186430311}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186430285} :answer-field/id #uuid "111bbd61-ed5a-5717-8d1a-2107732df5dc" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186430341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b020d76e-e1ef-5bcd-91cd-80bb99bd3362" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186430312} {:answer/id #uuid "b66681db-9ca9-5aa2-be1a-2b2722e717f0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{3}" :db/id 17592186430318} {:answer/id #uuid "e79293f1-0fa4-5fd9-a0c9-d75bdda1898a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}_{3}" :db/id 17592186430332}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186430318} :answer-field/id #uuid "290dfa59-387c-585b-835b-10031ed8be97" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186430342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2248db21-760b-5d89-a87a-6804c865097b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0" :db/id 17592186430266} {:answer/id #uuid "6853169f-45fb-53e5-9733-7e6d2c7b857b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}-{x}_{3}=0" :db/id 17592186430289} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd4ef4e-ed29-538c-9ad2-b749e4b9e1e3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/