</table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then

- $Σ$ is a $3\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,

- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\times 3$ matrix,

- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\times 2$ matrix.

From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\sigma }_{1}=\sqrt{5}$ and ${\sigma }_{2}=0.$
Also, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$

Therefore, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\frac{1}{{\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\  & =\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 2 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 0\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}\begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 2 \\ 0\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} \\ 0\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Since the second singular value is ${\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find vectors 

$$
u=\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ {x}_{3}\end{bmatrix}
$$

such that ${u}_{1}\cdot u=0$ and $‖u‖=1.$

Solving ${u}_{1}\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to

$$
\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}{x}_{2}=0\,⟹\,{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0,
$$

we get the general solution 

$$
\begin{bmatrix}-2{x}_{2} \\ {x}_{2} \\ {x}_{3}\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}{{\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\ 1 \\ 0\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{3}{{\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 0 \\ 1\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}},
$$

where ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables.

Notice that the two linearly independent solutions ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ are mutually orthogonal. Therefore, we only need to normalize them. This gives the second and third columns of $U:$   

$$
{u}_{2}=\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ 0\end{bmatrix}\,{u}_{3}=\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 0 \\ 1\end{bmatrix}
$$

So, the matrix $U$ could be the following:

$$
U=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} & -\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} & \frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186443408 :question/id #uuid "dd93c01d-3a4b-5e26-802f-bf34131bc696" :question/math-academy-id "q-363664" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31349149-08bd-53c6-9790-133dc7f5909c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186443332} {:answer/id #uuid "5de404de-f9b7-5dcf-ac57-f91f9957b36e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186443344} {:answer/id #uuid "69452e64-abf8-591a-a3d7-07720185da50" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{\sqrt{10}}" :db/id 17592186443348} {:answer/id #uuid "b8c5740c-7b0b-5df5-aa14-6fc680d3ae4b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{3}{\sqrt{10}}" :db/id 17592186443363}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186443332} :answer-field/id #uuid "00eaf422-de51-5a43-85c1-1733b5dc804e" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186443387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "014504c3-0095-55b6-8054-cf1b5f903c3b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{3}{\sqrt{10}}" :db/id 17592186443316} {:answer/id #uuid "01fd3847-5484-52af-91c0-9b24a43a0040" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\frac{1}{\sqrt{10}}" :db/id 17592186443317} {:answer/id #uuid "0a9ccc10-d0e7-5504-803b-00853a390c1b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{\sqrt{10}}" :db/id 17592186443321} {:answer/id #uuid "236d274a-ad0d-527a-a4cb-c76405b7556b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186443328}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186443321} :answer-field/id #uuid "1625078f-2b7e-5b8e-93f3-7f5ccc7d8e94" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186443389} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67e49303-f618-5401-90f4-c3f4a5f17e27" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{1}" :db/id 17592186443347} {:answer/id #uuid "6d04b951-79c5-5704-905e-29cb89e1e3ec" :ans