$$

Consider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the $3$rd column of the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then

- $Σ$ is a $3\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,

- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\times 3$ matrix,

- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\times 2$ matrix.

From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\sigma }_{1}=\sqrt{5}$ and ${\sigma }_{2}=2.$
Also, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$

Therefore, we can compute the $1$st and $2$nd columns of $U$ as follows:

- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\frac{1}{{\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\  & =\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\ -2 & 0 \\ -1 & 0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 0\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ -2 \\ -1\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ -\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} \\ -\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\frac{1}{{\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\  & =\frac{1}{2}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\ -2 & 0 \\ -1 & 0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 1\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\frac{1}{2}\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ 0 \\ 0\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 0 \\ 0\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Since we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the third column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector 

$$
{u}_{3}=\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ {x}_{3}\end{bmatrix}
$$

such that 

$$
\{\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\cdot {u}_{3}=0 \\ {u}_{2}\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\end{aligned}\,‖{u}_{3}‖=1.
$$

Solving this system, which is equivalent to

$$
\{\begin{aligned}-\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}{x}_{2}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}{x}_{3}=0 \\ {x}_{1}=0\end{aligned}\,⟹\,\{\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\ {x}_{1}=0,\end{aligned}
$$

we get the nonzero normalized solution 

$$
{u}_{3}=\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ -\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}\end{bmatrix}.
$$

Finally, we construct the matrix $U:$

$$
U=\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\ -\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} & 0 & -\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ -\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}\end{bmatrix}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186371429 :question/id #uuid "5dfe9dfb-2de9-5049-bb36-b64e2c2a8946" :question/math-academy-id "q-98770"} {:db/id 17592186371436 :question/id #uuid "1fbce2d1-be2d-5c6a-bfaf-0486d4c0daa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-98772" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186162043 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b36c482-75a0-5413-8e3e-4a72e3ddb26a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Factor in the SVD of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3ca5a0b-c8af-5e70-962f-1f5f6f4b7f7d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\ 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186371438} {:answer/id #uuid "1a8785d7-c5ad-518a-acd1-9f9ada9bd015" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 0 \\ 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186371439} {:answer/id #uuid "88254370-bfae-5dc3-81e7-adc53cf53476" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{3} \\ -\frac{2}{3} \\ \frac{2}{3}\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186371440} {:answer/id #uuid "7be15a9b-8f59-5064-9812-d260abe9e0d9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 0 \\ 1\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186371441} {:answer/id #uuid "2cc59cf3-c247-5942-a9f5-c1997970aef5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ 0\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186371442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88254370-bfae-5dc3-81e7-adc53cf53476" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{3} \\ -\frac{2}{3} \\ \frac{2}{3}\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186371440} :answer-field/id #uuid "77e9283f-fec6-5979-96c1-f6617f8a4d62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186371437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "$$
