</table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then

- $Σ$ is a $3\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,

- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\times 3$ matrix,

- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\times 2$ matrix.

From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\sigma }_{1}=5$ and ${\sigma }_{2}=0.$
Also, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$

Therefore, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:

$$
\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\frac{1}{{\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\  & =\frac{1}{5}\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\ -2 & 4 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\frac{1}{5}\begin{bmatrix}-\sqrt{5} \\ 2\sqrt{5} \\ 0\end{bmatrix} \\  & =\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} \\ 0\end{bmatrix}\end{aligned}
$$

Since the second singular value is ${\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find vectors 

$$
u=\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\ {x}_{2} \\ {x}_{3}\end{bmatrix}
$$

such that ${u}_{1}\cdot u=0$ and $‖u‖=1.$

Solving ${u}_{1}\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to

$$
-\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}{x}_{2}=0\,⟹\,-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0,
$$

we get the general solution 

$$
\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\ {x}_{2} \\ {x}_{3}\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}{{\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ 1 \\ 0\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{3}{{\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 0 \\ 1\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}},
$$

where ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables.

Notice that the two linearly independent solutions ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ are mutually orthogonal. Therefore, we only need to normalize them. This gives the second and third columns of $U:$   

$$
{u}_{2}=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ 0\end{bmatrix}\,{u}_{3}=\begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 0 \\ 1\end{bmatrix}
$$

So, the matrix $U$ could be the following:

$$
U=\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} & \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} & \frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "e6c10cae-3311-5de0-80be-f4f348e2b025" :step/next {:db/id 17592186408022}} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2078b66-2ae5-54f6-a460-e22e75e77234" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186407979} {:answer/id #uuid "a891a29c-280f-5600-bd3a-be3e4b2b01f3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186407982} {:answer/id #uuid "a9578c71-fcde-5fb5-a17c-8cd3bb804565" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{3}" :db/id 17592186407983}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186407982} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b9c438d-d68e-55fe-84e3-f15c3a21c90f" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186408000} {:answer/id #uuid "a2078b66-2ae5-54f6-a460-e22e75e77234" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186407979} {:answer/id #uuid "a891a29c-280f-5600-bd3a-be3e4b2b01f3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186407982} {:answer/id #uuid "a9578c71-fcde-5fb5-a17c-8cd3bb804565" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{3}" :db/id 17592186407983} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11957032-84d5-5287-bd1c-5e6f76cf0b6b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}" :db/id 17592186407931} {:answer/id #uuid "89bc27fe-361d-55f9-8ddc-0f93f93b8b48" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186407970} {:answer/id #uuid "8fcb6f12-af61-54ef-b3a4-e5cdbd213eb8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186407972} {:answer/id #uuid "a70a374b-4aab-5db4-9f20-c387df22f82c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}" :db/id 17592186407981}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186407981} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cf930fc-e7fc-5a60-856d-576c2a81a972" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186408001} {:answer/id #uuid "11957032-8