A=\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 2 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\,Σ=\begin{bmatrix}\sqrt{5} & 0 \\ 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\,V=\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}
$$

Consider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$  select the correct options in the computations of the matrix $U$ below.

From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce the singular values ${\sigma }_{1}=\sqrt{5}$ and ${\sigma }_{2}=0.$

Now, we compute the $1$st column of $U.$ It is given by:

|  |  | $\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}$ |  |  |
