We can use Riemann sums to approximate arc lengths. Let's see an example." :tutorial/id #uuid "c6c4aa50-1ce8-52f8-aa97-b2bce6c85623" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7614 :tutorial/title "Arc Length"} :step/id #uuid "4da87fab-f669-5510-93d3-55fea59cbf65" :step/math-academy-id 44210 :step/next {:db/id 17592186193532}} {:db/id 17592186193831 :tutorial/content "We've seen how to use Riemann sums to approximate areas under curves of composite functions. Our final task is determining whether these approximations overestimate or underestimate the true areas.

