We can approximate the integral above using a *left* Riemann sum with $3$ equal subintervals and step size $Δx$ as follows:

$$
{\int }_{0}^{9}g(x)\,\text{d}x≈(g(0)+g(3)+g(6)\cdot Δx
$$

Now, we set up a table with values of $g(x)$ at each point:

| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| ${f}^{′}(x)$ | $2\sqrt{2}$ | $0$ | $4\sqrt{3}$ | $\sqrt{3}$ |
| $g(x)=\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}$ | $3$ | $1$ | $7$ | $2$ |

Finally, we obtain the following approximation for our arc length:

$$
\begin{aligned}L & ={\int }_{0}^{9}g(x)\,\text{d}x \\  & ≈(g(0)+g(3)+g(6))\cdot Δx \\  & =(3+1+7)\cdot 3 \\  & =11\cdot 3 \\  & =33\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "e5bc175d-e11b-55ff-aaea-33f654704c94" :step/next {:db/id 17592186510511}} {:db/id 17592186510511 :step/content {:db/id 17592186510395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "190b0318-472c-530a-9953-285c1d80e520" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186509737} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff2cf17-07cf-5a9d-b5df-c3c58e89ffd3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186510023} {:answer/id #uuid "cd101352-2412-5c2e-9e18-8982229905ae" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186510119} {:answer/id #uuid "d0bd2120-8fb6-53d0-90aa-f72e30d237ae" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186510131} {:answer/id #uuid "e99d7e0b-5dd6-505c-adc8-246fea845a95" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186510191}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186510023} :answer-field/id #uuid "bda027a4-fbea-5ab2-9b7c-09170115f2b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186510336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "597bb006-761e-5b6e-a002-be65431d8129" :question/math-academy-id "q-149505" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be negative and strictly increasing for $x\in [0,1],$ and differentiable for $x\in (0,1).$ Suppose we approximate the area under the curve $y=g(x)=({x}^{2}-2)\cdot f(x)$ over the interval $[0,1]$ using a right Riemann sum. Given that $g(x)>0,$ which of the following statements must be true?

I. ${f}^{′}(x)>0$

II. ${g}^{′}(x)>0$

III. The Riemann sum underestimates the true area." :question/worked-solution "We're given that $g(x)=({x}^{2}-2)\cdot f(x)>0.$ Now, recall the following:

- If $g(x)$ is strictly increasing, the right Riemann sum gives an *overestimate* of the area under the curve $y=g(x).$

- If $g(x)$ is strictly decreasing, the right Riemann sum gives an *underestimate* of the area under the curve $y=g(x).$

Let's now consider each statement in turn:

- Statement I is true. Since $f(x)$ is strictly increasing, we have ${f}^{′}(x)>0.$

- Statement II is false. Differentiating $g(x)=({x}^{2}-2)\cdot f(x),$ we get

$$
\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2}-2)^{′}\cdot f(x)+({x}^{2}-2)\cdot {f}^{′}(x) \\  & =2x\cdot f(x)+({x}^{2}-2)\cdot {f}^{′}(x).\end{aligned}
$$

Now, since $f(x)$ is negative and strictly increasing over the interval $(0,1),$ we have 

$$
2x>0,\,f(x)<0,\,{x}^{2}-2<0,\,{f}^{′}(x)>0.
$$

Hence, we obtain

$$
{g}^{′}(x)={{2x}_{⏟}}_{>0}\cdot {{f(x)}_{⏟}}_{<0}+{{({x}^{2}-2)}_{⏟}}_{<0}\cdot {{{f}^{′}(x)}_{⏟}}_{>0}={{2x\cdot f(x)}_{⏟}}_{<0}+\,{{{x}^{2}\cdot {f}^{′}(x)}_{⏟}}_{<0}<0.
$$

- Statement III is true. Since ${g}^{′}(x)<0,$ the function $g(x)$ is strictly decreasing. Therefore, the right Riemann sum gives an *underestimate* of the area under the curve $y=({x}^{2}-2)\cdot f(x).$

Therefore, the correct answer is "I and III only.""} :step/id #uuid "694eb003-d786-5734-a959-cc83c41aa69e"} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "190b0318-472c-530a-9953-285c1d80e520" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186509737} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff2cf17-07cf-5a9d-b5df-c3c58e89ffd3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186510023} {:answer/id #uuid "cd101352-2412-5c2e-9e18-8982229905ae" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186510119} {:answer/id #uuid "d0bd2120-8fb6-53d0-90aa-f72e30d237ae" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186510131} {:answer/id #uuid "e99d7e0b-5dd6-505c-adc8-246fea845a95" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186510191}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186510023} :answer-field/id #uuid "bda027a4-fbea-5ab2-9b7c-09170115f2b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186510336} {:answer/id #uuid "190b0318-472c-530a-9953-285c1d80e520" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186509737} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff2cf17-07cf-5a9d-b5df-c3c58e89ffd3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186510023} {:answer/id #uuid "cd101352-2412-5c2e-9e18-8982229905ae" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186510119} {:answer/id #uuid "d0bd2120-8fb6-53d0-90aa-f72e30d237ae" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186510131} {:answer/id #uuid "e99d7e0b-5dd6-505c-adc8-246fea845a95" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186510191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87f7157d-9ee6-5b05-9ef8-654c1987e877" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186190049} {:answer/id #uuid "b36c179e-6374-5bb0-8b12-b5bd9f9953b2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186190050} {:answer/id #uuid "d278bfce-4eb5-553f-8225-33457823e6d0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186190051} {:answer/id #uuid "1309590e-1bde-5aa8-8965-b5de6255f2c3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the statements must be true." :db/id 17592186190052} {:answer/id #uuid "7bfc40b4-1eb7-5831-886c-c91fce39b4d5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id 17592186190053}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186190053} :answer-field/id #uuid "277d264b-fac7-5d04-a619-a104e80d1d5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186190048} {:answer/id #uuid "87f7157d-9ee6-5b05-9ef8-654c1987e877" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186190049} {:answer/id #uuid "b36c179e-6374-5bb0-8b12-b5bd9f9953b2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186190050} {:answer/id #uuid "d278bfce-4eb5-553f-8225-33457823e6d0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186190051} {:answer/id #uuid "1309590e-1bde-5aa8-8965-b5de6255f2c3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the statements must be true." :db/id 17592186190052} {:answer/id #uuid "7bfc40b4-1eb7-5831-886c-c91fce39b4d5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id 17592186190053} {:db/id 17592186510539 :step/content {:db/id 17592186510425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14818b9f-c464-5b94-bee6-e801c16f016a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "48\pi " :db/id 17592186509725} {:answer/id #uuid "4b983bb9-6a3a-5849-8009-b5191583e3f6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "64\pi " :db/id 17592186509843} {:answer/id #uuid "55d254e1-55ef-55c0-a7d5-3dadc286794f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "24\pi " :db/id 17592186509865} {:answer/id #uuid "657b83be-229f-5a37-a103-a6cbf918ce96" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "32\pi " :db/id 17592186509898} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4c20a8-cc6f-5131-826d-a35ace3db5e0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "36\pi " :db/id 17592186510224}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186509725} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a53dba6-93aa-5232-bd89-2d7c6d8b683b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186510297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "95ecf8d2-2252-5516-85e1-ebd3d6544d2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-149419" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of a positive, continuous function $f(x)$ over the closed interval $[0,15].$ 
Using a right Riemann sum with $5$ equal subintervals, estimate the volume of the solid generated when the region bounded by the curve $y=f(x),$ the $x$-axis, and the vertical lines $x=0$ and $x=15$ is rotated $2\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis.

| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ | $12$ | $15$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| $f(x)$ | $3$ | $2$ | $\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $2\sqrt{2}$ | $1$ |

*Hint: The volume of the solid generated when the region bounded by a curve $y=f(x),$ the $x$-axis, and the vertical lines $x=a$ and $x=b$ is rotated $2\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis is given by*

$$
V=\pi {\int }_{a}^{b}[f(x)]^{2}\,\text{d}x.
$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, the volume of the solid generated when the region bounded by a curve $y=f(x),$ the $x$-axis, and the vertical lines $x=0$ and $x=15$ is rotated $2\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis is given by

$$
V=\pi {\int }_{0}^{15}[f(x)]^{2}\,\text{d}x.
$$

Let $g(x)={(f(x))}^{2}.$ The (regular) step size $Δx$ is given by 

$$
Δx=\frac{15-0}{5}=3.
$$

We can approximate the integral above using a *right* Riemann sum with $5$ equal subintervals and step size $Δx$ as follows:

$$
\pi {\int }_{0}^{15}g(x)\,\text{d}x≈\pi \cdot (g(3)+g(6)+g(9)+g(12)+g(15))\cdot Δx
$$

We set up a table with values of $g(x)$ at each point:

| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ | $12$ | $15$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| $f(x)$ | $3$ | $2$ | $\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $2\sqrt{2}$ | $1$ |
| $g(x)={(f(x))}^{2}$ | $9$ | $4$ | $3$ | $0$ | $8$ | $1$ |

Finally, we obtain the following approximation for our volume:

$$
\begin{aligned}V & =\pi {\int }_{0}^{15}g(x)\,\text{d}x \\  & ≈\pi \cdot (g(3)+g(6)+g(9)+g(12)+g(15))\cdot Δx \\  & =\pi \cdot (4+3+0+8+1)\cdot 3 \\  & =\pi \cdot 16\cdot 3 \\  & =48\pi \end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "c0e73eb7-4739-5f4b-84a0-6fccb98ec129" :step/next {:db/id 17592186510490}} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14818b9f-c464-5b94-bee6-e801c16f016a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "48\pi " :db/id 17592186509725} {:answer/id #uuid "4b983bb9-6a3a-5849-8009-b5191583e3f6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "64\pi " :db/id 17592186509843} {:answer/id #uuid "55d254e1-55ef-55c0-a7d5-3dadc286794f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "24\pi " :db/id 17592186509865} {:answer/id #uuid "657b83be-229f-5a37-a103-a6cbf918ce96" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "32\pi " :db/id 17592186509898} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4c20a8-cc6f-5131-826d-a35ace3db5e0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "36\pi " :db/id 17592186510224}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186509725} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a53dba6-93aa-5232-bd89-2d7c6d8b683b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186510297} {:answer/id #uuid "14818b9f-c464-5b94-bee6-e801c16f016a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "48\pi " :db/id 17592186509725} {:answer/id #uuid "4b983bb9-6a3a-5849-8009-b5191583e3f6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "64\pi " :db/id 17592186509843} {:answer/id #uuid "55d254e1-55ef-55c0-a7d5-3dadc286794f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "24\pi " :db/id 17592186509865} {:answer/id #uuid "657b83be-229f-5a37-a103-a6cbf918ce96" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "32\pi " :db/id 17592186509898} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4c20a8-cc6f-5131-826d-a35ace3db5e0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "36\pi " :db/id 17592186510224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f63c264-1a0f-552a-b8ad-9620bc2188c1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id 17592186509718} {:answer/id #uuid "13fe11c3-e0ca-520e-8103-0b01e9b72896" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db