d/id #uuid "e2fca817-6a22-5c0a-8bd9-eb65ba7787e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186126637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49e9a4ed-cc02-552b-850f-590a1eabb508" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{25}{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186374008} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6da4e6-4d70-5d57-830d-2c3550356100" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{25}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186374009} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c418fd-e2e2-58e2-b16d-b624dda6a4c9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{5}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186374010} {:answer/id #uuid "0d81db19-07f6-520d-bd7f-8449d3b4156e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{5}{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186374011} {:answer/id #uuid "91e95a72-f432-5a4d-9e2e-324cee6736c0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{5}{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186374012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91e95a72-f432-5a4d-9e2e-324cee6736c0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{5}{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186374012} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d2f399-c08f-57b6-b31d-d84d8b9705c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186374007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=25.$
Express the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. 

$$
{∭}_{R}\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\,\text{d}V
$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form

$$
{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\,f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\,{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.
$$

If $(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:

$$
x=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,y=\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,z=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ
$$

Notice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $5$ centered at the origin. 
As a result, in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as 

$$
Δ={(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)\,:\,0\le \rho \le 5,\,0\le \theta \le 2\pi ,\,0\le ϕ\le \pi }.
$$

Next, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & =\frac{\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\cdot \rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{{\rho }^{2}} \\  & =\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  

$$
\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\,\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\cdot {\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{5}{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186129756 :question/id #uuid "5e21b1a1-dd1a-5b1e-a6f4-aca8044792b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-40073" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186129264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7a75441-d233-5a64-8d87-b3138c2d31be" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9282e885-d570-5d72-9968-8527160b169f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\displaystyle \int_{0}^{π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{9}ρ 3 sin ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id 17592186128018} {:answer/id #uuid "048690e5-c379-58d8-ac2f-79765dfd32aa" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\displaystyle \int_{0}^{π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{3}ρ 4 cos ⁡ ϕ sin ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id 17592186128019} {:answer/id #uuid "528058ee-b8cf-5ca5-b635-c49112468757" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\displaystyle \int_{0}^{π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{3}ρ 3 sin ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id 17592186128020} {:answer/id #uuid "57d1d358-75e3-59df-80ce-35c3d6d36295" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2 π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{3}ρ 4 cos ⁡ ϕ sin ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id 17592186128021} {:answer/id #uuid "66a974b1-4913-5a37-a4cb-eda26703eb43" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2 π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2π}\displaystyle \int_{0}^{3}ρ 4 cos ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id 17592186128022}] :answer-field/id #uuid "167cbf2b-6403-547f-9f10-b1af15a48555" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186128017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aa22172-aed4-5605-92ab-59f3b9c082a8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{4}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186375137} {:answer/id #uuid "47674ef2-eb40-5ead-b7da-b61decf7c865" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{9}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186375138} {:answer/id #uuid "a76f3460-fc95-508d-924f-bca258671c28" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{4}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186375139} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0a05b0-be97-5bf2-ae2d-2d653d7ac4e7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186375140} {:answer/id #uuid "6976b7cc-768c-59b4-88b8-9e266d9b514a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{4}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186375141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6976b7cc-768c-59b4-88b8-9e266d9b514a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{4}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186375141} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d1c327d-1302-5a46-953f-a8e3268dd875" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186375136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9.$
Express the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. 

$$
{∭}_{R}z\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\,\text{d}V
$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form

$$
{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\,f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\,{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.
$$

If $(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:

$$
x=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,y=\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,z=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ
$$

Notice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $3$ centered at the origin. 
As a result, in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as 

$$
Δ={(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)\,:\,0\le \rho \le 3,\,0\le \theta \le 2\pi ,\,0\le ϕ\le \pi }.
$$

Next, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=z\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & =\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\cdot \rho  \\  & ={\rho }^{2}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  

$$
\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}z\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\,\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\cdot {\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{4}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186373993 :question/id #uuid "52a77714-a767-5195-b412-fb970a316089" :question/math-academy-id "q-161747"} {:db/id 17592186374013 :question/id #uuid "351698ef-ed69-59a8-a86e-a782ca5a2c9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161756"} {:db/id 17592186374034 :question/id #uuid "af7b91cf-b6cb-5d8f-879b-0e99c7144b05" :question/math-academy-id "q-161761"} {:db/id 17592186482510 :question/id #uuid "1521c62d-edb7-5cf4-9412-1fda40e8b968" :question/math-academy-id "q-161758"} {:db/id 17592186482521 :question/id #uuid "31ed4558-6b89-5259-81f7-c1113b514f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161755"} {:db/id 17592186482558 :question/id #uuid "80477a9d-e7af-5d9c-aba6-cf99ec36f94b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161762"} {:db/id 17592186482576 :question/id #uuid "ac302ee6-6bbe-5388-bf60-4247113c7536" :question/math-academy-id "q-161750"} {:db/id 17592186482583 :question/id #uuid "b6dfd2f6-e989-5dc0-8a5f-19807faa0173" :question/math-academy-id "q-161743"} {:db/id 17592186496299 :question/id #uuid "b06611cf-54db-58f0-8277-482f7aa27724" :question/math-academy-id "q-161753" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19b76607-eca3-5a84-8112-1e82b79c1646" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\sqrt{3}}{\rho }^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495561} {:answer/id #uuid "3454506d-b82b-5713-b11f-01ee75904e1f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{4}\operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495633} {:answer/id #uuid "37432da4-1104-5db3-8f3f-d145e4ff681b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\sqrt{3}}{\rho }^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495638} {:answer/id #uuid "c1695142-7e5b-54c7-a0c8-e74c43072eb0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495936} {:answer/id #uuid "c737b74c-b7cd-528f-8697-a21b09e1b183" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\sqrt{3}}{\rho }^{5}{sin}^{2}⁡\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495946}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186495946} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb52fe98-2353-5c03-b8bc-f23854e8e611" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186496167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=3.$
Express the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. 

$$
{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\,\text{d}V
$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form

$$
{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\,f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\,{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.
$$

If $(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:

$$
x=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,y=\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,z=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ
$$

Notice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $\sqrt{3}$ centered at the origin. 
As a result, in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as 

$$
Δ=\{(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)\,:\,0\le \rho \le \sqrt{3},\,0\le \theta \le 2\pi ,\,0\le ϕ\le \pi \}.
$$

Next, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)={y}^{2}\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & =(\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2}\cdot \rho  \\  & ={\rho }^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  

$$
\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\,\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\rho }^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\cdot {\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\sqrt{3}}{\rho }^{5}{sin}^{2}⁡\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186129265 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186128842 :question/id #uuid "c56b3218-2c96-59fe-a5e3-af6f01164af4" :question/math-academy-id "e-11373"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b1d5b6a-3e7b-567d-a61f-d18f55924912" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186129758 :question/id #uuid "1a921fbf-9bfb-5cd0-be15-5730003e7ec3" :question/math-academy-id "q-40089"} {:db/id 17592186129759 :question/id #uuid "182369a1-0318-58db-8fc8-603690ab0d2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-40152"} {:db/id 17592186374076 :question/id #uuid "2cc017fc-6823-51fb-9163-20f65438f28e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161859"} {:db/id 17592186374104 :question/id #uuid "da25fda3-5d77-5ee4-8008-42f6ecb3ae06" :question/math-academy-id "q-161919"} {:db/id 17592186374111 :question/id #uuid "6dea07d3-2087-5531-b95a-ce86e560c57c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161920"} {:db/id 17592186374118 :question/id #uuid "dedd8b4a-01ea-5c5c-b27b-c92c5e8a483c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161924"} {:db/id 17592186482552 :question/id #uuid "75e6fbad-2ffa-554a-b73e-206d1de35163" :question/math-academy-id "q-161921"} {:db/id 17592186482566 :question/id #uuid "934f832d-975f-5cb5-827f-5f4ce2444543" :question/math-academy-id "q-161918"} {:db/id 17592186482585 :question/id #uuid "ba16213a-d9f2-5675-b515-f66161bd7267" :question/math-academy-id "q-161922"} {:db/id 17592186482607 :question/id #uuid "e9ac6b1f-2b21-59f9-9ae8-01d7811a1b26" :question/math-academy-id "q-161861"} {:db/id 17592186496318 :question/id #uuid "e3dbf795-87d9-5ee7-946c-df26586b5ee5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161860"}] :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Shifted Sphere"} {:db/id 17592186128842 :question/id #uuid "c56b3218-2c96-59fe-a5e3-af6f01164af4" :question/math-academy-id "e-11373"} {:db/id 17592186129758 :question/id #uuid "1a921fbf-9bfb-5cd0-be15-5730003e7ec3" :question/math-academy-id "q-40089"} {:db/id 17592186129759 :question/id #uuid "182369a1-0318-58db-8fc8-603690ab0d2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-40152"} {:db/id 17592186374076 :question/id #uuid "2cc017fc-6823-51fb-9163-20f65438f28e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161859"} {:db/id 17592186374104 :question/id #uuid "da25fda3-5d77-5ee4-8008-42f6ecb3ae06" :question/math-academy-id "q-161919"} {:db/id 17592186374111 :question/id #uuid "6dea07d3-2087-5531-b95a-ce86e560c57c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161920"} {:db/id 17592186374118 :question/id #uuid "dedd8b4a-01ea-5c5c-b27b-c92c5e8a483c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161924"} {:db/id 17592186482552 :question/id #uuid "75e6fbad-2ffa-554a-b73e-206d1de35163" :question/math-academy-id "q-161921"} {:db/id 17592186482566 :question/id #uuid "934f832d-975f-5cb5-827f-5f4ce2444543" :question/math-academy-id "q-161918"} {:db/id 17592186482585 :question/id #uuid "ba16213a-d9f2-5675-b515-f66161bd7267" :question/math-academy-id "q-161922"} {:db/id 17592186482607 :question/id #uuid "e9ac6b1f-2b21-59f9-9ae8-01d7811a1b26" :question/math-academy-id "q-161861"} {:db/id 17592186496318 :question/id #uuid "e3dbf795-87d9-5ee7-946c-df26586b5ee5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161860" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c3d150-55f6-525d-b55a-6951b89555eb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "${\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{4\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ$ v" :db/id 17592186495516} {:answer/id #uuid "0641edc9-9f46-539c-b517-a7dff5678e4b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{8\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495527} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7b57ca-d67c-5580-9698-a81cf1ce11e0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{8\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{\rho }^{3}{sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495813} {:answer/id #uuid "9a52e985-8c43-591c-a2b1-487e13e3bbcf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "${\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{8\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ$ v" :db/id 17592186495854} {:answer/id #uuid "b2362d0a-41f0-5512-8b16-672410d72346" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{4\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{\rho }^{3}{sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495912}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186495527} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cbd266d-a5fa-5b3b-84b2-668b33154b73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186496094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d2a71ffdce7f02cdfa78881c7e355c9aada4134cf06b663a2deefb3d779b9ca.png)

The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=8x,$ shown above. 
Express the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. 

$$
{∭}_{R}y\,\text{d}V
$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form

$$
{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\,f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\,{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.
$$

If $(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:

$$
x=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,y=\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,z=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ
$$

Notice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $4$ centered at $(4,0,0).$

With that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=8x$ in spherical polar coordinates:

$$
\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =8x \\ {\rho }^{2} & =8\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ \\ \rho (\rho -8\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) & =0\end{aligned}
$$



Since $\rho $ cannot be identical to zero on the entire sphere, we must have $\rho =8\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$

![](images/04/0475e2e272a30318dc4cb31457539a312544b6e14d7e6a8ed3f911d41404b575.png)



As a result, we obtain that in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as 

$$
Δ=\{(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)\,:\,0\le \rho \le 8\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,-\frac{\pi }{2}\le \theta \le \frac{\pi }{2},\,0\le ϕ\le \pi \}.
$$

Next, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=y:$

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & =\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  

$$
\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}y\,\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\cdot {\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{8\operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{sin}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186129266 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186128843 :question/id #uuid "85182b2a-10d4-5663-831b-41623c395cce" :question/math-academy-id "e-11374"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ea201b-cf90-54cf-bd20-d7e990345710" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186129749 :question/id #uuid "c69820a4-d58d-582a-b52f-9dd9aeb08800" :question/math-academy-id "q-39665"} {:db/id 17592186129761 :question/id #uuid "0dc6df5e-ab71-5282-9ee2-65cc548d41a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-40155"} {:db/id 17592186371961 :question/id #uuid "6e23e7ac-d75a-538e-9787-5d9be89e54a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161597"} {:db/id 17592186374048 :question/id #uuid "09d71fff-9588-5c81-88c5-d8db5fd3b138" :question/math-academy-id "q-161767"} {:db/id 17592186374055 :question/id #uuid "8033cac6-a02e-5637-a33a-ed6c8951714d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161769"} {:db/id 17592186374062 :question/id #uuid "16e3144c-e694-5291-82ca-3ee165563da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161778"} {:db/id 17592186374069 :question/id #uuid "e845cebe-7731-5881-96fa-918a8775c3a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161790"} {:db/id 17592186482504 :question/id #uuid "0136e908-03ab-5353-9218-7031e36c58ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-161787"} {:db/id 17592186482535 :question/id #uuid "4913e4d1-197e-5ba9-a574-72530dddbf74" :question/math-academy-id "q-161789"} {:db/id 17592186482601 :question/id #uuid "ddc59e97-e243-5e27-9d57-5e0f9b714882" :question/math-academy-id "q-161777"} {:db/id 17592186496307 :question/id #uuid "c2868a77-a9f6-5df5-bf81-a733f20b3a9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161765"} {:db/id 17592186496308 :question/id #uuid "c4c2ec08-50ad-518f-bd3d-48075268a2f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161771"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral by Converting to Spherical Polar Coordinates"} {:db/id 17592186128843 :question/id #uuid "85182b2a-10d4-5663-831b-41623c395cce" :question/math-academy-id "e-11374"} {:db/id 17592186129749 :question/id #uuid "c69820a4-d58d-582a-b52f-9dd9aeb08800" :question/math-academy-id "q-39665"} {:db/id 17592186129761 :question/id #uuid "0dc6df5e-ab71-5282-9ee2-65cc548d41a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-40155"} {:db/id 17592186371961 :question/id #uuid "6e23e7ac-d75a-538e-9787-5d9be89e54a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161597"} {:db/id 17592186374048 :question/id #uuid "09d71fff-9588-5c81-88c5-d8db5fd3b138" :question/math-academy-id "q-161767"} {:db/id 17592186374055 :question/id #uuid "8033cac6-a02e-5637-a33a-ed6c8951714d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161769"} {:db/id 17592186374062 :question/id #uuid "16e3144c-e694-5291-82ca-3ee165563da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161778"} {:db/id 17592186374069 :question/id #uuid "e845cebe-7731-5881-96fa-918a8775c3a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161790"} {:db/id 17592186482504 :question/id #uuid "0136e908-03ab-5353-9218-7031e36c58ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-161787"} {:db/id 17592186482535 :question/id #uuid "4913e4d1-197e-5ba9-a574-72530dddbf74" :question/math-academy-id "q-161789"} {:db/id 17592186482601 :question/id #uuid "ddc59e97-e243-5e27-9d57-5e0f9b714882" :question/math-academy-id "q-161777"} {:db/id 17592186496307 :question/id #uuid "c2868a77-a9f6-5df5-bf81-a733f20b3a9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161765" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0782d6f6-9606-57ec-9b7b-5f331ab47d02" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{36\pi }{5}" :db/id 17592186495529} {:answer/id #uuid "844ba137-ce42-54c2-ad73-0a6795c8a9ff" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{128\pi }{15}" :db/id 17592186495794} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e1bc82-3dca-5d12-a26c-e853c58acc81" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{256\pi }{81}" :db/id 17592186495972} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f9f8b0-bd2d-567a-a334-e4d0096c528c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{81\pi }{8}" :db/id 17592186495983} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f5beda-e35c-5b36-a994-c61647e4e3cc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{64\pi }{27}" :db/id 17592186496046}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186495794} :answer-field/id #uuid "452ba3e6-053b-531a-8d38-cad4a5db1e22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186496108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral

$$
{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\,\text{d}V
$$

over the region $R$ enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form

$$
{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\,f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\,{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.
$$

If $(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:

$$
x=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,y=\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,z=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ
$$

Notice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $2$ centered at the origin. 
As a result, in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as 

$$
Δ=\{(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)\,:\,0\le \rho \le 2,\,0\le \theta \le 2\pi ,\,0\le ϕ\le \pi \}.
$$

Next, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)={z}^{2}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & =(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & ={\rho }^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}z\,\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\rho }^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\cdot {\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2}{\rho }^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,dϕ\cdot {\int }_{0}^{2\pi }d\theta \cdot {\int }_{0}^{2}{\rho }^{4}\,d\rho  \\  & ={[-\frac{1}{3}{cos}^{3}⁡ϕ]}_{ϕ=0}^{ϕ=\pi }\cdot [\theta ]_{\theta =0}^{\theta =2\pi }\cdot {[\frac{1}{5}{\rho }^{5}]}_{\rho =0}^{\rho =2}\,d\rho  \\  & =-\frac{1}{3}(-1-1)\cdot (2\pi -0)\cdot \frac{1}{5}(32-0) \\  & =\frac{2}{3}\cdot 2\pi \cdot \frac{32}{5} \\  & =\frac{128\pi }{15}\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186496308 :question/id #uuid "c4c2ec08-50ad-518f-bd3d-48075268a2f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161771" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021f15c9-f5ca-5fc3-8d40-1a3115937ceb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{128\pi }{7}" :db/id 17592186495513} {:answer/id #uuid "02d47acc-5e12-5a9c-bd05-2023d477bc45" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "25\pi " :db/id 17592186495517} {:answer/id #uuid "18832182-39dc-5364-9464-ffd9aaaa5c09" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{64\pi }{3}" :db/id 17592186495557} {:answer/id #uuid "821f4bda-e9cb-5812-adda-f108cac57aa9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "16\pi " :db/id 17592186495789} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e840a3-e6d2-5b8d-b91c-2840c23ac88b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{81\pi }{4}" :db/id 17592186495881}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186495513} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f2e7f56-ee2d-5dfd-af32-c2c72dce6d2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186496079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "![](images/2f/2fd023af7c229d813344ee366b384a5917b69df0d06fabff6466b9ebcc199bb9.png)

Evaluate the triple integral

$$
{∭}_{R}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{2}\,\text{d}V
$$

over the region $R$ enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ for $y\le 0$ and $z\le 0,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form

$$
{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\,f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\,{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.
$$

If $(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:

$$
x=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,y=\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,z=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ
$$

Notice that the region $R$ represents one-quarter of the sphere of radius $2$ centered at the origin.

![](images/09/090f210768ffd4a6be529860b54a2906e265427b7d85bcbb07e3101c801740ba.png)



As a result, we obtain that in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as 

$$
Δ=\{(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)\,:\,0\le \rho \le 2,\,\pi \le \theta \le 2\pi ,\,\frac{\pi }{2}\le ϕ\le \pi \}.
$$

Next, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)={({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{2}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & ={({\rho }^{2})}^{2} \\  & ={\rho }^{4}\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{2}\,\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\rho }^{4}\cdot {\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{\pi /2}^{\pi }{\int }_{\pi }^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2}{\rho }^{6}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{\pi /2}^{\pi }\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,dϕ\cdot {\int }_{\pi }^{2\pi }d\theta \cdot {\int }_{0}^{2}{\rho }^{6}\,d\rho  \\  & =[-\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ]_{ϕ=\pi /2}^{ϕ=\pi }\cdot [\theta ]_{\theta =\pi }^{\theta =2\pi }\cdot {[\frac{1}{7}{\rho }^{7}]}_{\rho =0}^{\rho =2} \\  & =-(-1-0)\cdot (2\pi -\pi )\cdot \frac{1}{7}(128-0) \\  & =1\cdot \pi \cdot \frac{128}{7} \\  & =\frac{128\pi }{7}\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186129281 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186128859 :question/id #uuid "2adb62b7-c889-5c4c-be0f-8f26a240475c" :question/math-academy-id "e-12409"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d85b11c-498d-53b7-98f8-b742b46e8dc2" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186129524 :question/id #uuid "afaacfe7-897b-552c-9b79-61482abf35f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161766"} {:db/id 17592186129760 :question/id #uuid "4dc06060-1fda-590b-bf44-a946ea904294" :question/math-academy-id "q-40154"} {:db/id 17592186374000 :question/id #uuid "282a7de5-01ec-5bdd-ad49-145c8d84d2bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161748"} {:db/id 17592186374020 :question/id #uuid "ac3d7303-e14a-5571-9831-0eb03f695bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161757"} {:db/id 17592186374027 :question/id #uuid "79d3cb68-3e16-5f1e-b189-33638dfa47d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161760"} {:db/id 17592186374041 :question/id #uuid "735e8926-bcf2-5559-be83-81f81871a7cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161763"} {:db/id 17592186482512 :question/id #uuid "164ec461-433f-5d34-8b46-e1e7c87d7fe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161759"} {:db/id 17592186482536 :question/id #uuid "4a047214-1415-5946-9ec9-da29ccac571a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161774"} {:db/id 17592186482587 :question/id #uuid "bbdf7ac8-9c8d-5122-94b8-607404da611a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161768"} {:db/id 17592186482590 :question/id #uuid "ca85c537-9f01-5979-bc36-583972546691" :question/math-academy-id "q-161773"} {:db/id 17592186496227 :question/id #uuid "07d5c9c5-374d-5c01-b3ec-d01486174f96" :question/math-academy-id "q-161744"}] :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Part-Sphere"} {:db/id 17592186128859 :question/id #uuid "2adb62b7-c889-5c4c-be0f-8f26a240475c" :question/math-academy-id "e-12409"} {:db/id 17592186129524 :question/id #uuid "afaacfe7-897b-552c-9b79-61482abf35f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161766"} {:db/id 17592186129760 :question/id #uuid "4dc06060-1fda-590b-bf44-a946ea904294" :question/math-academy-id "q-40154"} {:db/id 17592186374000 :question/id #uuid "282a7de5-01ec-5bdd-ad49-145c8d84d2bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161748"} {:db/id 17592186374020 :question/id #uuid "ac3d7303-e14a-5571-9831-0eb03f695bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161757"} {:db/id 17592186374027 :question/id #uuid "79d3cb68-3e16-5f1e-b189-33638dfa47d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161760"} {:db/id 17592186374041 :question/id #uuid "735e8926-bcf2-5559-be83-81f81871a7cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161763"} {:db/id 17592186482512 :question/id #uuid "164ec461-433f-5d34-8b46-e1e7c87d7fe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161759"} {:db/id 17592186482536 :question/id #uuid "4a047214-1415-5946-9ec9-da29ccac571a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161774"} {:db/id 17592186482587 :question/id #uuid "bbdf7ac8-9c8d-5122-94b8-607404da611a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161768"} {:db/id 17592186482590 :question/id #uuid "ca85c537-9f01-5979-bc36-583972546691" :question/math-academy-id "q-161773"} {:db/id 17592186496227 :question/id #uuid "07d5c9c5-374d-5c01-b3ec-d01486174f96" :question/math-academy-id "q-161744" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a717243-48be-536d-910a-6d83ab68f329" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495536} {:answer/id #uuid "1afd572b-1bde-5282-aebe-538e26120c34" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495564} {:answer/id #uuid "5a35fc1c-68fd-5d54-b891-f97bb27891a2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495714} {:answer/id #uuid "90820d05-7799-52ea-bb46-3e07581e83ec" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495829} {:answer/id #uuid "cf09a2be-f3f1-58fe-aff8-83664e28906f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495963}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186495829} :answer-field/id #uuid "851dbeb9-5199-5c05-92dd-f09fe944b1b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186496139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9$ for $x\ge 0.$
Express the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. 

$$
{∭}_{R}\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\,\text{d}V
$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form

$$
{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\,f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\,{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.
$$

If $(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:

$$
x=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,y=\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,z=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ
$$

Notice that the region $R$ represents one-half of the sphere of radius $3$ centered at the origin.

![](images/d2/d2b9c6f3541c47f37ad7f2ba52d739787e39600ec71fe3530f0ad2846c24880b.png)



As a result, we obtain that in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as 

$$
Δ=\{(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)\,:\,0\le \rho \le 3,\,-\frac{\pi }{2}\le \theta \le \frac{\pi }{2},\,0\le ϕ\le \pi \}.
$$

Next, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & =\sqrt{(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2}+(\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2}} \\  & =\sqrt{{\rho }^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ} \\  & =\sqrt{{\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ({cos}^{2}⁡\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\theta )} \\  & =\sqrt{{\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ} \\  & =\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  

$$
\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\,\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\cdot {\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.\end{aligned}
