$$"} :step/id #uuid "63749430-c9f6-5d26-a7e1-481aa4f8c432" :step/next {:db/id 17592186496363}} {:db/id 17592186496363 :step/content {:db/id 17592186496308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021f15c9-f5ca-5fc3-8d40-1a3115937ceb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{128\pi }{7}" :db/id 17592186495513} {:answer/id #uuid "02d47acc-5e12-5a9c-bd05-2023d477bc45" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "25\pi " :db/id 17592186495517} {:answer/id #uuid "18832182-39dc-5364-9464-ffd9aaaa5c09" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{64\pi }{3}" :db/id 17592186495557} {:answer/id #uuid "821f4bda-e9cb-5812-adda-f108cac57aa9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "16\pi " :db/id 17592186495789} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e840a3-e6d2-5b8d-b91c-2840c23ac88b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{81\pi }{4}" :db/id 17592186495881}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186495513} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f2e7f56-ee2d-5dfd-af32-c2c72dce6d2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186496079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c4c2ec08-50ad-518f-bd3d-48075268a2f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161771" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2fd023af7c229d813344ee366b384a5917b69df0d06fabff6466b9ebcc199bb9.png)

Evaluate the triple integral

$$
{∭}_{R}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{2}\,\text{d}V
$$

over the region $R$ enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ for $y\le 0$ and $z\le 0,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form

$$
{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\,f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\,{\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.
$$

If $(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:

$$
x=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,y=\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\,z=\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ
$$

Notice that the region $R$ represents one-quarter of the sphere of radius $2$ centered at the origin.

![](images/09/090f210768ffd4a6be529860b54a2906e265427b7d85bcbb07e3101c801740ba.png)



As a result, we obtain that in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as 

$$
Δ=\{(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)\,:\,0\le \rho \le 2,\,\pi \le \theta \le 2\pi ,\,\frac{\pi }{2}\le ϕ\le \pi \}.
$$

Next, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)={({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{2}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & ={({\rho }^{2})}^{2} \\  & ={\rho }^{4}\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{2}\,\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\rho }^{4}\cdot {\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{\pi /2}^{\pi }{\int }_{\pi }^{2\pi }{\int }_{0}^{2}{\rho }^{6}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{\pi /2}^{\pi }\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,dϕ\cdot {\int }_{\pi }^{2\pi }d\theta \cdot {\int }_{0}^{2}{\rho }^{6}\,d\rho  \\  & =[-\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ]_{ϕ=\pi /2}^{ϕ=\pi }\cdot [\theta ]_{\theta =\pi }^{\theta =2\pi }\cdot {[\frac{1}{7}{\rho }^{7}]}_{\rho =0}^{\rho =2} \\  & =-(-1-0)\cdot (2\pi -\pi )\cdot \frac{1}{7}(128-0) \\  & =1\cdot \pi \cdot \frac{128}{7} \\  & =\frac{128\pi }{7}\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "8b10d38c-406c-548c-b35d-cf1e229f05a8" :step/next {:db/id 17592186496378}} {:db/id 17592186496371 :step/content {:db/id 17592186496227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a717243-48be-536d-910a-6d83ab68f329" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495536} {:answer/id #uuid "1afd572b-1bde-5282-aebe-538e26120c34" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495564} {:answer/id #uuid "5a35fc1c-68fd-5d54-b891-f97bb27891a2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{0}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495714} {:answer/id #uuid "90820d05-7799-52ea-bb46-3e07581e83ec" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495829} {:answer/id #uuid "cf09a2be-f3f1-58fe-aff8-83664e28906f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ" :db/id 17592186495963}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186495829} :answer-field/id #uuid "851dbeb9-5199-5c05-92dd-f09fe944b1b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186496139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "07d5c9c5-374d-5c01-b3ec-d01486174f96" :question/math-academy-id "q-161744" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9$ for $x\ge 0.$
