![](images/d2/d2b9c6f3541c47f37ad7f2ba52d739787e39600ec71fe3530f0ad2846c24880b.png)



As a result, we obtain that in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as 

$$
Δ=\{(\rho ,\theta ,ϕ)\,:\,0\le \rho \le 3,\,-\frac{\pi }{2}\le \theta \le \frac{\pi }{2},\,0\le ϕ\le \pi \}.
$$

Next, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}:$

$$
\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\  & =\sqrt{(\rho \operatorname{cos}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2}+(\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡\theta \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2}} \\  & =\sqrt{{\rho }^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ} \\  & =\sqrt{{\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ({cos}^{2}⁡\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\theta )} \\  & =\sqrt{{\rho }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ} \\  & =\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  

$$
\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\,\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\rho \operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\cdot {\rho }^{2}\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ \\  & ={\int }_{0}^{\pi }{\int }_{-\pi /2}^{\pi /2}{\int }_{0}^{3}{\rho }^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\,d\rho \,d\theta \,dϕ.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "a5f82725-c8bc-52c2-b33d-594e53b847fb" :step/next {:db/id 17592186496375}} {:db/id 17592186496352 :step/content {:db/id 17592186496307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0782d6f6-9606-57ec-9b7b-5f331ab47d02" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{36\pi }{5}" :db/id 17592186495529} {:answer/id #uuid "844ba137-ce42-54c2-ad73-0a6795c8a9ff" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{128\pi }{15}" :db/id 17592186495794} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e1bc82-3dca-5d12-a26c-e853c58acc81" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{256\pi }{81}" :db/id 17592186495972} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f9f8b0-bd2d-567a-a334-e4d0096c528c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{81\pi }{8}" :db/id 17592186495983} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f5beda-e35c-5b36-a994-c61647e4e3cc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{64\pi }{27}" :db/id 17592186496046}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186495794} :answer-field/id #uuid "452ba3e6-053b-531a-8d38-cad4a5db1e22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186496108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c2868a77-a9f6-5df5-bf81-a733f20b3a9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161765" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral

