$$
f(x)∼\frac{\pi }{2}-{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{4}{\pi (2n-1)^{2}}\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)x).
$$

Select the correct options in the reasoning below.

At $x=0,$ we have

$$
\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)\cdot 0)={{field-1}}.
$$

Since $f(x)$ is 
{{field-2}}
at $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to 

$$
f(0)={{field-3}}.
$$

Therefore, we have 

$$
{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}={{field-4}}.
$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as

$$
f(x)∼\frac{\pi }{2}-\frac{4}{\pi }{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\cdot \operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)x).
$$

Now, notice that at $x=0,$ we have

$$
\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)\cdot 0)=\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.
$$

Since $f(x)$ is $\text{continuous}$ at $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to 

$$
f(0)=0.
$$



Therefore, we have 

$$
\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\frac{\pi }{2}-\frac{4}{\pi }{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\cdot \operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)\cdot 0) \\ 0 & =\frac{\pi }{2}-\frac{4}{\pi }{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\cdot 1 \\ -\frac{\pi }{2} & =-\frac{4}{\pi }{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} \\ {\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} & =\frac{{\pi }^{2}}{8}.\end{aligned}
$$"} :step/id #uuid "953b546a-265d-5b9a-a212-47ea85583cca" :step/next {:db/id 17592186506625}} {:db/id 17592186506649 :step/content {:db/id 17592186402320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59e944d4-7bfb-518e-9bee-2fdf150f8144" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-1)^{n+1}" :db/id 17592186402322} {:answer/id #uuid "47de1570-9f8f-50d0-b18a-c75ae926d19e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186402323} {:answer/id #uuid "8dcea2a2-3096-50e6-a6b7-e9b80e1e8393" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186402324} {:answer/id #uuid "c33a2222-b813-50a8-a34a-21f9fa0adc40" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-1)^{n}" :db/id 17592186402325}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186402325} :answer-field/id #uuid "99fb0232-8fde-57f4-8464-e80e09aee727" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186402321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "936b6cfe-f0ac-576f-a3dc-b5ba23f06fe2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186402327} {:answer/id #uuid "70839883-5fc1-5247-a1fc-3be76986282f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id 17592186402328} {:answer/id #uuid "f1246f30-4357-529f-8208-4e10b1450218" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186402329}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186402328} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd8b7d7-7185-5a90-873c-4b6de94753ee" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186402326} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b9d6515-49bb-5976-8c6c-5bd6c5d69d0e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{\pi }^{2}}{8}" :db/id 17592186402331} {:answer/id #uuid "a8fdc5a5-d940-5536-903a-a3af45edabd9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{\pi }{2}" :db/id 17592186402332} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e2473f-6d10-58cd-9c2d-75974fbf25c4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{\pi }{4}" :db/id 17592186402333} {:answer/id #uuid "2219bdb7-7b65-5c58-8ff5-e35d8409d539" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\frac{{\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id 17592186402334}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186402333} :answer-field/id #uuid "e257c7be-72fa-5044-afd5-3c231c4d2101" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186402330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d961e8a-0a6f-54c1-8cde-ab0903529501" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id 17592186402336} {:answer/id #uuid "c6754a7b-081e-5d31-992c-2069f9dc057c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499} :answer/value "discontinuous" :db/id 17592186402337}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186402336} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b9f9176-6990-5c20-b84c-e134dd361960" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186402335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9937b4b8-0233-5d12-b8c0-111d5bfd92fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-343445" :question/problem "$$
F(x)=\{\begin{aligned}-4, & x\in [-\pi ,0] \\ 2, & x\in (0,\pi )\end{aligned}
$$

Consider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by

$$
f(x)∼-1+{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{12}{\pi (2n-1)}sin\,((2n-1)x).
$$

Select the correct options in the reasoning below.

At $x=-\frac{\pi }{2},$ we have

$$
sin\,((2n-1)\cdot (-\frac{\pi }{2}))={{field-1}}.
$$

Since $f(x)$ is 
{{field-2}}
at $x=-\frac{\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to 

$$
f(-\frac{\pi }{2})={{field-3}}.
$$

Therefore, we have 

$$
{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.
$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as

$$
f(x)∼-1+\frac{12}{\pi }{\sum }_{n=1}^{\infty }\frac{1}{2n-1}\cdot sin\,((2n-1)x).
$$

Now, notice that at $x=-\frac{\pi }{2},$ we have

$$
sin\,((2n-1)\cdot (-\frac{\pi }{2}))=sin\,(\frac{\pi }{2}-n\pi )=(-1)^{n}.
$$

Since $f(x)$ is $\text{continuous}$ at $x=-\frac{\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to 

$$
f(-\frac{\pi }{2})=-4.
$$



