The function $y=f(x)$ above is defined and continuous on the closed interval $x\in [-5,2].$ By filling the blank spaces in the sentence below, complete the statement of the intermediate value theorem:

*If $k$ is a number that lies between $\textrm{ ________ }$ inclusively, then there exists a number $c \in [-5,2]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-5,2],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(-5)$ and $f(2).$

Since $f(-5)=1$ and $f(2)=4$, we must have $k\in[1,4].$

Therefore, the missing part is "$1$ and $4$". The complete sentence is:

*If $k$ is a number that lies between $1$ and $4$ inclusively, then there exists a number $c \in [-5,2]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*"} {:db/id 17592186134476 :question/id #uuid "69dfc1c5-3195-5cf2-bc4a-740b775a4bef" :question/math-academy-id "q-48343" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186133832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d01d143-68f2-534a-8be6-4f63f9ab0d40" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Statement On the Intermediate Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e50f37f-de04-5f77-ba2f-0ee2ac1b3b70" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II, III" :db/id 17592186132895} {:answer/id #uuid "e97b8ed1-34bd-5695-ad22-e12a6cc61fba" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III, II" :db/id 17592186132896} {:answer/id #uuid "fa53d2ea-c1bd-5aa5-965f-9513e9eaafc7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, III" :db/id 17592186132897} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7c910c-3f13-51d6-bee7-ce0c300dfe90" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II, I" :db/id 17592186132898} {:answer/id #uuid "3a9192d3-9f25-57bd-a508-793119bd9a59" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II" :db/id 17592186132899}] :answer-field/id #uuid "16a5fed7-59bc-5485-b040-90f121190eda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186132894}] :question/problem "A statement of the intermediate value theorem is given below but some of its parts are missing.

