t/id #uuid "6388d315-340b-56a0-bc93-e380bfbf6ed3" :knowledge-point/title "Selecting a Specific Value For Which a Solution Is Guaranteed"}] :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=(x-3)^2+2.$ According to the intermediate value theorem, for which values of $k$ does the equation $f(x)=k$ have a guaranteed solution on the interval $[2,6]?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by plotting the function.

