If we plot the function, we can get an idea of why the intermediate value theorem cannot be applied.

![](images/9b/9b9543ec11b350cea4ca18e24a8db6ae8f72ffc38e64f973f9af2f83f1226400.png)

The graph shows that, for example, the equation $f(x)=1.5$ has no solution on $[1,4]$ despite the fact that $1.5$ lies between $f(1)=4$ and $f(4)=0.$
So, the intermediate value theorem does not hold.

**Watch out!** The interval on which we apply the intermediate value theorem must *always* be closed. For example, we can't apply the theorem on an interval like $[1,3).$" :tutorial/id #uuid "a6571cd4-d390-5e75-907d-726b500e6976" :tutorial/math-academy-id 309 :tutorial/title "Why Does the Function Have to Be Continuous?"} {:db/id 17592186134979 :step/content {:db/id 17592186133957 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186133481 :question/id #uuid "89750383-d5a6-5bf4-b6b2-abd489e44d3c" :question/math-academy-id "e-116"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1012ae9a-26d6-50bf-a46a-7c859d856752" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186051076}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186134472} {:db/id 17592186134473} {:db/id 17592186241118} {:db/id 17592186329800} {:db/id 17592186329801} {:db/id 17592186329803} {:db/id 17592186398834}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals On Which the IVT Can Be Applied"} :step/id #uuid "79d4ad5d-f388-5fc5-a8b7-a72f14369138" :step/math-academy-id 571}] "attributes" [[10 :db/ident :db.type/keyword :db.cardinality/one] [11 :db.install/partition :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [13 :db.install/attribute :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [15 :db/excise :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/one] [16 :db.excise/attrs :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [17 :db.excise/beforeT :db.type/long :db.cardinality/one] [18 :db.excise/before :db.type/instant :db.cardinality/one] [19 :db.alter/attribute :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/many] [40 :db/valueType :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/one] [41 :db/cardinality :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/one] [42 :db/unique :db.type/ref :db.cardinality/one] [43 :db/isComponent :db.type/boolean :db.cardinality/one] [44 :db/index :db.type/boolean :db.cardinality/one] [45 :db/noHistory :db.type/boolean :db.cardinality/one] [50 :db/txInstant :db.type/instant :db.cardinality/one] [51 :db/fulltext :db.type/boolean :db.cardinality/one] [52 :db/fn :db.type/fn :db.cardinality/one] [62 :db/doc :db.type/string :db.ca