$$
-5 \leq 2x+3 \leq 5
$$

Now, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods:

$$
-5 \le 2x + 3 \le 5; - 8 \le 2x \le 2; - 4 \le x \le 1
$$" 17592186045417] [17592186070026 1065 8825 17592186045417] [17592186070026 1066 #uuid "53ecd5cc-486a-584d-abc8-f75ec26f12cc" 17592186045417] [17592186070026 1067 "Introduction" 17592186045417] [17592186070027 1064 "We take a similar approach for absolute value inequalities involving the "greater than" symbol. To illustrate, consider the following absolute value inequality:

