![](images/29/29a81db4068e5bcc97fd38729ca19f11988a08e905bfc189e69c88357185ea31.svg)

in $\mathbb{R^2}$ are orthogonal, since

$$
\begin{aligned}{e}_{1}\cdot {e}_{2} & =\begin{bmatrix}1 \\ 0\end{bmatrix}\cdot \begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 1\end{bmatrix} \\  & =1\cdot 0+0\cdot 1 \\  & =0+0 \\  & =0.\end{aligned}
$$

