e1c-488592b9d60c" 17592186045417] [17592186193694 1063 17592186193904 17592186045417] [17592186193695 1058 17592186193532 17592186045417] [17592186193695 1061 44210 17592186045417] [17592186193695 1062 #uuid "4da87fab-f669-5510-93d3-55fea59cbf65" 17592186045417] [17592186193695 1063 17592186193905 17592186045417] [17592186193827 1064 "In this lesson, we'll learn how to use Riemann sums to approximate definite integrals of *composite* functions. As we'll see, this has some interesting applications.

For example, suppose $f(x)$ is a positive, continuous function. Some values for $f(x)$ over the interval $x\in [1,5]$ are given by the following table:

| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |
