$$
X_1, X_2, \ldots, X_{n} \sim N(\mu,\sigma^2).
$$

In this case, we can easily determine the sampling distribution of the sample mean

$$
\overline{X} = \dfrac{1}{n} \sum\limits_{i=1}^n X_i.
$$

Recall the following:

- The sum of $n$ independent and identically distributed normal random variables is normally distributed. Thus, 

$$
Y = \displaystyle \sum\limits_{i=1}^n X_i
$$

is normally distributed.

- A normally distributed random variable scaled by a constant factor is normally distributed. Thus, 

$$
\overline{X} = \dfrac1n\cdot Y
$$

is normally distributed.

Also, we previously saw that the expected value of the sample mean equals the population mean, i.e., 

$$
\textrm{E}[\overline{X}] = \mu,
$$

and the variance of the sample mean is

$$
\textrm{Var}[\overline{X}] = \dfrac{\sigma^2}{n}.
$$

Putting all of this together, we obtain that

$$
\overline{X} \sim N\left(\mu, \dfrac{\sigma^2}{n}\right),
$$

In other words, the sample mean $\overline{X}$ is normally distributed with mean $\mu$ and variance $\dfrac{\sigma^2}{n}.$" 17592186045417] [17592186163327 1065 6277 17592186045417] [17592186163327 1066 #uuid "14d0c44e-7b46-50e5-800f-e73c03b66e46" 17592186045417] [17592186163327 1067 "Introduction" 17592186045417] [17592186421578 1080 "0.0047" 17592186045417] [17592186421578 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186421578 1083 #uuid "65f2abb0-f4a9-5c49-b1bf-402f28d52bc7" 17592186045417] [17592186421579 1080 "0.0055" 17592186045417] [17592186421579 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186421579 1083 #uuid "6c55880a-7dc0-5d85-971e-c6e7ea95264d" 17592186045417] [17592186421580 1080 "0.0060" 17592186045417] [17592186421580 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186421580 1083 #uuid "7158a375-0ebf-5d37-976b-e42ece269ac1" 17592186045417] [17592186421590 1080 "0.0033" 17592186045417] [17592186421590 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186421590 1083 #uuid "a3ff9bc9-da2b-5dd6-ab09-e1939754ca30" 17592186045417] [17592186421596 1080 "0.0062" 17592186045417] [17592186421596 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186421596 1083 #uuid "b31a223e-b919-56fb-b210-1641a36a0596" 17592186045417] [17592186421621 1075 17592186421578 17592186045417] [17592186421621 1075 17592186421579 17592186045417] [17592186421621 1075 17592186421580 17592186045417] [17592186421621 1075 17592186421590 17592186045417] [17592186421621 1075 17592186421596 17592186045417] [17592186421621 1076 17592186045493 17592186045417] [17592186421621 1077 "selection" 17592186045417] [17592186421621 1078 17592186421596 17592186045417] [17592186421621 1079 #uuid "ecd948f6-0fc7-557e-95fe-81a08ab35f83" 17592186045417] [17592186421628 1068 17592186421621 17592186045417] [17592186421628 1069 "q-143455" 17592186045417] [17592186421628 1070 17592186045486 17592186045417] [17592186421628 1071 "The volumes of soda in cans filled in at a particular factory are normally distributed with a mean of $12\,\text{oz